par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @The Port of Peri Peri\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Vietnamese\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Mounika\u8217?s place\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Sunday \u8226? 10-25-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up @3am, played mobile games, fed the cats, made salt coffee, made and ate breakfast, washed dishes, cat litter, studied system design, made and ate lunch, washed dishes, put some shoes in storage, sorted some souvenirs, finished watching my mini YT series on finding a needle in a haystack, showed Val the finished website, napped, worked out, picked up some McDonalds\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Study system design\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @McDonalds\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Saturday \u8226? 10-24-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up @3am. Made breakfast for Val, fed the cats, reached out to Steve for work, worked on me and Val\u8217?s website, showered, did some self care, made and ate breakfast, plan grocery shopping, budgeted, watched YT, studied system design, fed the cats, helped Val w groceries, made and ate lunch, watched Love on the Spectrum, over napped to the point where we couldn\u8217?t go workout, ran laundry, then watched more Love on the Spectrum, then went to sleep.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Budget\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Friday \u8226? 10-23-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up, litter, ate breakfast, applied for unemployment, laundry, threw away luggage, sorted souvenirs, washed dishes, filled in information for my doctor\u8217?s appointment, napped, went to get some chipotle and watched Love on the Spectrum, took another nap, woke up, then went back to sleep. A slow day today catching up on sleep.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Applied for unemployment\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Chipotle\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Thursday \u8226? 10-22-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up, ate breakfast, got gas and some kolaches from Bucees, then headed to Dallas. I arrived then started unpacking. Showed Val my souvenirs, took a nap, then woke up to go to a haunted house. After the haunted house, we went to in n out to eat, then a coffee shop which was also a bar, we got gas then headed home.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Gas\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Drive to Dallas\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Home\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Haunted house\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   In-n-out\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   La Reunion\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Gas\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Wednesday \u8226? 10-21-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 27 in Vietnam. Day 2 in Ho Chi Minh City. Last day in Vietnam \u-10179?\u-9068? Woke up, ate a banh mi dad bought, then went to get a coffee @Highlands coffee. Went home, finished packing then headed to the airport. Waited for a couple of hours @ the airport trying to be productive updating my Vietnamese notes, finishing me and Val\u8217?s website and planning mom\u8217?s website, then got on the flight back home to Taiwan. I finished watching Ready Player One and Bumblebee. We waited for two hours for our next flight, we got on, and headed back to Houston. I finished The 15:17 to Paris then tried to sleep for the rest of the flight which was difficult. The rest of the flight was rough and I couldn\u8217?t get much rest. We got to the airport, got a uber, then headed home. Our driver was Vietnamese and I spoke w him ab Vietnam. He was 39 years old and he was an uber driver w 2 kids. We got home and started unpacking then got a haircut, showered, then went to sleep.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Highlands coffee\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Flight to Taiwan\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Flight to Houston\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Home\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Haircut\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Tuesday \u8226? 10-20-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 26 in Vietnam. Day 1 in Ho Chi Minh City. Woke up, got ready, then headed to dad\u8217?s sister\u8217?s house in Son Qui. We ate breakfast first and i had chow at this restaurant that like a pond where you could fish from. We ate then headed out to meet my dad\u8217?s sister. We arrive, sat down and talked for a bit w my dad\u8217?s sister. She was nice and ~14 years older than my dad. They told me a funny story how my dad and his sister Anh walked ~20 mins away. Dad picked up a pile of sand and dropped it. The wind brought the sand to his eye and he started crying. They both went back to the house and dad said his sister did it. Mom then beat his sister lol. We sat down talking for a bit then when we were leaving they made us pray. We then left and headed home. Before going home we stopped by a com tam place and picked it up so we can eat at home. We went home and ate. I showered then relaxed. There was a father w his two daughters playing piano downstairs so my dad told me to come down and play. We talked and connected on playing the piano. I played la Campanella and she freaked out when I played the beginning. We chatted for a bit then they left. Me and dad went to go get a massage. We got a massage then left to go get coffee. We saw a couple w a pet cat and they dressed him up in a shirt. We drank a salt coffee then headed back to the house. I went to bed but it was hard for me to fall asleep. 3.6k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Breakfast @H\u7891? c\u226?u c\u225? gi\u7843?i tr\u237? + Nh\u224? H\u224?ng Ho\u224?n T\u226?n\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dad\u8217?s sister\u8217?s house\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Phuc\u8217?s house\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Massage\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Highlands coffee\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Monday \u8226? 10-19-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 25 in Vietnam. Day 4 in Hanoi. I woke up late ~9am since we were drinking last night. I then headed out @10am to go to a friend\u8217?s place to hangout w him. Then I left to aunt\u8217?s coffee shop to catch up w her and drink some tea. We then went to get a banh mi next to the coffee shop and I ate it at the coffee shop. After finishing my sandwich, I went to go to a railroad coffee shop but I was stopped by the receptionist and went to a coffee shop she recommended. We talked for a bit then headed to the hotel to grab my luggage to bring to my aunt\u8217?s coffee shop. I arrived to the coffee shop and said goodbye to my new friend, so sad. I then took a shower at my aunt\u8217?s place then went downstairs to go eat. We tried to eat fried tofu but everyone went on their lunch break so we went to go eat red noodles. It was the first time eating on a chair. We then made our way back to the coffee shop and ordered the driver. The driver arrived then I headed to the airport. I sat down waiting to get on the plane. I got on the plane and headed toward HCMC. I arrived then got a grab to my parent\u8217?s location. We then went out to eat dinner @ a restaurant nearby and I told them ab my trip to Hanoi. We walked back to dad\u8217?s place, showered, then went to sleep. 7.9k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Friend\u8217?s place\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   LAI\u8217?s coffee shop\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Breakfast @B\u225?nh m\u236? heo quay _ Rim B\u225?nh M\u236?\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Mallard | Coffee and Music Mallard coffee\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   LAI\u8217?s coffee shop\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Nh\u224? H\u224?ng Song Ph\u7889?\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Airport\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Flight to Ho Chi Minh City\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Phuc\u8217?s house\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Nh\u224? h\u224?ng C\u226?y S\u7913?\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Phuc\u8217?s house\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Sunday \u8226? 10-18-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 24 in Vietnam. Day 3 in Hanoi. I woke up around 8am which is late for me since I wanted to sleep in. I got ready then headed out to start my day. I got dirty clothes and wanted to run laundry since I don\u8217?t have any more clean underwear. I then walked over to a famous coffee shop that sold egg coffee where I met someone from France. He was 18 years old solo traveling Asia. He\u8217?s only been to Laos n Vietnam. I tried to sit upstairs however it was too packed for me to even see. I then walked around browsing random stores then walked back to my aunt\u8217?s coffee shop. She gave me a chocolate milk then we went out to eat brunch. She is quite confident and reminds me of a Vietnamese woman. She gave me a warmer nuoc mam. We finished eating then we went back to the coffee shop but she stopped by two places to buy some things for her. We drank some tea and talked a bit ab religion, politics and family. I then left to the temple of literature took pics then headed out to the museum of fine arts. It was quite big but they didn\u8217?t have much AC. I then got a grab to a pagoda next to the lake. I got in and took pics and I saw someone\u8217?s family having a funeral due to white headbands on their heads. There were little creatures in water bottles and I thought that was interesting. I also bought some golden bills to give as gift to my friends and family. I then got a grab back to the hotel and the guy tried to get an extra 10k from me. I relaxed for a bit before walking out to the lake. I also bought some water puppet tickets but they ended up being for tomorrow so I\u8217?ll probably give them to my new friend. I got to the lake then started to walk around to find a coffee shop. I got some egg coffee for the second time today but it wasn\u8217?t as good. Quite bitter without a nice view. I then left looking for another coffee but I ended up running into the water puppet show and I\u8217?m so happy that I bought more tickets to it. The show was great and unique. I\u8217?ve never seen a show like this before and it was quite the experience. I went to walk over to a restaurant where me and my friends planned to meet up and eat. We ate Bun Thang and we talked for a bit. We then headed out to drink beer and snack on some finger food. We sat in the middle beer street and started eating drinking and hanging out. All of the sudden everyone is scrambling out of their seats and packing up tables and chairs. In Vietnam there is a new rule where you cannot sit in the middle of the street or sidewalk to keep it clean. It reminded me of New York w the chaotic energy. We drank and ate a lot before my new friend had to leave since he had classes in the morning. Me and the couple went to another beer spot and we drank and talked to each other. We also met someone from Nepal who is a computer engineer. We drank then we left. It was a sad goodbye. I then walked home then headed out to drink some coffee since I still had a buzz. I finished my coffee and enjoyed myself then went back to the hotel and went to sleep. I\u8217?m going to miss Vietnam. It seems much similar. People are just worried about having a good time. Even the night I just had was amazing. We drank and I never worried about the money. All I was worried about was how I felt, how drunk I was, the realest journal I\u8217?ve made this trip due to the fact I am currently drunk. I\u8217?m currently out right now sitting next to the cathedral hoping to make some friends. This could be a lifestyle, however this is my last day here. The number of friends I\u8217?ve made already have been intentional. I cannot wait to make more. The fact this city can offer than is insane. I made three great friends tonight. Two from Czech Republic and one from Vietnam. They will come to the US and I will invite them over. This has been one of my favorite days in Vietnam bc I am drunk. This could be a lifestyle and the only reason why is bc im w friends. I cannot wait to drink here again. Ppl respect the rules here greatly. 20.6k steps\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Laundry\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Cafe \u272?inh\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   GINKGO T-shirts 49 Dinh Tien Hoang\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   LAI\u8217?s coffee\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Brunch @B\u225?nh Cu\u7889?n 101 B\u224? Tri\u7879?u\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   LAI\u8217?s coffee\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Temple Of Literature\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Vietnam National Fine Arts Museum\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Tran Quoc Pagoda\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Caf\u233? Gi\u7843?ng\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Water puppet show\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @B\u250?n Thang Lan L\u249?n\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Beer street\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Saturday \u8226? 10-17-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 23 in Vietnam. Day 2 in Hanoi. Go a grab to the hotel @3:30am, checked in, then went to sleep, woke up , then headed out to eat pho for breakfast, then headed over to get salt coffee w my aunt. We talked a bit then I headed out to find a good hotel w a cheap price. I ended up finding a cheap hotel for $16 a night and made a new friend in the process. We showered and rested a bit before heading out to explore the prison. They claim they treated the Americans fairly but n prison. Which was an interesting observation I made. I then took a grab to go to the flag tower but found out I had to pay for a ticket to explore the tower and 5 other attractions. I explored all of the attractions which was hot and took so long to walk around. I then took a grab to go eat where Obama ate. I met some Koreans who were visiting and were going to Sapa. I then started walking back to the hotel to rest but I ran into the walking street which was nice to experience since the US doesn\u8217?t have anything like this. My aunt texted me so I took a grab to her coffee shop.  We spoke for a bit before she dropped me off @ the hotel where I rested for a bit. I then headed out to meet w my new receptionist friend to show me around the night life. We walked around the street where I got a sugarcane juice while walking around the lake, night market and beer street. There were so many performers on the street. Ppl playing the violin, ppl dancing, dj\u8217?s, adidas grand opening, and we ran into the president of Vietnam and Switzerland. Beer street reminded me of Buy Vien street minus the dancing women. We walked back in the general area then I went back to the hotel. 27.7k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   St. Joseph Cathedral\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Breakfast @10 P. L\u253? Qu\u7889?c S\u432?\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   LAI's Coffee\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hoa Lo Prison Relic\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hanoi Flag Tower\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Imperial Citadel of Thang Long\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Giant Precious Sapphire Turtle\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Revolutionary Relic D67 Building and Bunker\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Gi\u7871?ng ng\u7921?\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   C\u7893?ng th\u224?nh\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Kinh Thien Palace\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @B\u250?n ch\u7843? H\u432?\u417?ng Li\u234?n\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   LAI\u8217?s coffee\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Ph\u7903? G\u224? Nguy\u7879?t\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Walking street\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Night market\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Beer street\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Friday \u8226? 10-16-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 22 in Vietnam. Day 3 in Ha Giang. Woke up, packed everything, then went to the first hostel we stayed at to drop off our luggage. We then stopped by a laundromat to wash my tour guide\u8217?s clothes. We then went to a pho spot to eat Ha Giang pho. We then drove to the border of Vietnam and China. I saw some locals and put \u8220?my friend likes bald men\u8221? to the Chinese ppl. We then walked to a conscience store to try Chinese beer, durian ice cream, and a spicy meat snack in a packet. We then went to a road where only scooter can go in and we stopped at a cafe, I tried to get salt coffee but they didn\u8217?t have any, so we just walked over a bridge to get to a waterfall. We took pics but didn\u8217?t get in the water. We made a mini damn, explored an abandoned house, then went to go eat lunch. We ate lunch then me and the tour guide\u8217?s swam at the pool there. It was cold but we got used to it after a while. We learned viet and English from each other then got dressed. We made friends w 2 other girls we met and they were quite interesting. They both spoke pretty good English. One was 28 and normal but the other was 19 and she was an odd ball. Should would talk about how no one understands her and that she got kicked out of the place she was volunteering at and that she is traveling around Vietnam w no money. We waited for the tour guide to come pick us up w his bike and me andWe then walked around for a bit enjoying the view then got on the bike to go to another waterfall. We swam and took pics for a bit enjoying the cold water. We tried getting to a higher ledge but it was too slippery to get on so we just chilled in the water. There were two other guys who looked like they were Japanese gangsters bc of their tats. I spoke w them for a bit before heading out. We headed to the hotel to relax for a bit but ended up going to a coffee shop to get salt coffee. There wasn\u8217?t anyone there initially so we sat upstairs and talked to the kid who was there playing Roblox. I talked w Tran for a while talking ab everything. I actually really like talking to this guy. He is very mature for only being 18. We then walked back to the hotel and we went out to eat dinner. We ate sour pho which didn\u8217?t have any broth which threw me off. We then went to another coffee shop w a nice view and I got a salt coffee. We then went back to the hotel and I tipped our tour guide. I showered then spoke w the receptionist for a bit then I got everything ready for the trip back to Hanoi. I got on the bus and I felt more confident this time coming back. 15.6k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Breakfast @Qu\u225?n b\u250?n Vi\u7871?t Xu\u226?n\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Vietnamese & Chinese border\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Coffee shop\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Waterfall\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Khu\u7893?i My Homestay\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Swim\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Walk\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Waterfall\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Coffee @Chay Coffee\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @PH\u7902? CHUA TRINHLY\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Coffee @Cafe N\u250?i C\u7845?m\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Sleeper bus to Hanoi\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Thursday \u8226? 10-15-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 21 in Vietnam. Day 2 in Ha Giang. Woke up, packed all my stuff then headed out to eat breakfast @B\u225?nh Cu\u244?\u769?n B\u224? H\u224?. We then got into the van and started our excursion. We stopped at a viewpoint w a great view, got a salt coffee w a view, got a ticket to a boat along the river and we took a bus shuttle down to the boat. We took pics and enjoyed the ride watching the scenery and wild animals, then took a bus shuttle back up to the ticket location, stopped @ a small coffee shop w a view, a grocery store, then dinner @ . We then checked into our hotel after saying bye to our other members of the group. I checked into then spent the rest of the night playing games, calling Val, and self care. 6.7k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Breakfast @B\u225?nh Cu\u244?\u769?n B\u224? H\u224?\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Coffee @Ma Pi Leng Panorama Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Boat ride @S\u244?ng Nho Qu\u7871?\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Ng\u7885?c Lan Qu\u225?n\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Coffee @C\u225?n Ty\u777? Panorama\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Nh\u224? h\u224?ng Vinh T\u432?\u7901?ng - G\u224? 9 ph\u250?t\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Wednesday \u8226? 10-14-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 20 in Vietnam. Day 1 in Ha Giang. We woke up, I got ready then we headed in the van to start our excursion. We stopped by a checkpoint that said 0km. Then we headed tog et breakfast @ a duck noodle restaurant native to Ha Giang. We made a couple of stops looking at mountain tits, a native old tall tree that is now rare, getting sugarcane juice, eating a native vegetable with meat wrapped around it, running into a traffic jam, an old house that was used in a film, a house that was designed w influence from the French, Vietnamese, and Chinese, the northernmost point of Vietnam, an ethnic village, and a flag point which we went to the top level. We then went to the old town where we will be staying the night. We at @ a local restaurant and tried black skinned chicken for the first time, then went back to the hotel. After showering and getting settled, we went out to walk around the old quarter where it was very lovely w music and ppl playing games. We stayed out and saw someone start a fire and then we danced around it. I stayed out for a bit longer than the other guys then headed back to hotel to sleep. 12.8k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Breakfast @B\u250?n V\u7883?t L\u224?ng H\u7919?u Th\u224?nh\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Coffee @C\u224? ph\u234? Ly San 1\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Ti\u7879?m C\u417?m L\u361?ng C\u7849?m\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Northernmost Point of Vietnam\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lo Lo village\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lung Cu Flag Point\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Nh\u224? h\u224?ng h\u7843?i hi\u7873?n\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Walking \u272?\u7891?ng V\u259?n Old Quarter\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Tuesday \u8226? 10-13-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 19 in Vietnam. Day 5 in Da Nang. Day 1 in Hanoi. Woke up, ate breakfast, back to the hotel room then went to the jewelry store to buy Carolyn\u8217?s bracelet. The driver picked me up in his car then we went to the store. I saw the precious lady that helped me before and it was a quick interaction. I bought the bracelet for $100 then went back to the hotel. I then picked up my shoes at the cleaners. It was hard to communicate w her since I didn\u8217?t have a ticket but she eventually found my shoes. I went back to the room to shower. I packed everything up then headed to the airport where I ate a beef and cheese banh mi @CIAS - B\u225?nh M\u236? Ph\u7889?. My flight got delayed by ~30 mins but then I met this older couple on the plane. I talked w them ab everything and it was nice talking w older ppl who reminded me of my parents. We landed then I went to pick up my luggage and met my driver outside. I took a short nap to the cafe so I could catch up on sleep. I had about an hour to explore Hanoi on my own so I took a grab to go to the opera house. I then walked around and ended up @ a lake exploring and taking pics around the area. I bought a $2 ticket to go into a temple that had a bridge to a religious site. I then took a grab back to the coffee shop where we went out to eat dinner. We talked for a bit and I got to know my aunt for the first time. She spoke very good English and I asked her questions about her personal life. We then went back to the coffee shop where I got my luggage then headed to the bus stop. It was my first time on a scooter and carrying luggage. I didn\u8217?t think I could do it but I did it hehe. We got there on time but the organizers purposefully gave an earlier time so that foreigners can make the bus on time. I got there @8pm but the bus gets here @8:30pm and nearly leaves @9pm. I got on and it gave hostel vibes. To Ha Giang we go! 9.6k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Jewelry store\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pick up shoes\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Airport\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Banh mi @CIAS - B\u225?nh M\u236? Ph\u7889?\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Flight to Hanoi\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   LAI's Coffee\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hanoi Opera House\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Ho\u224?n Ki\u7871?m Lake\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Ngoc Son Temple\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   LAI\u8217?s Coffee\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Ch\u7843? c\u225? L\u259?ng Thung C\u7845?m - 32 V\u245? Th\u7883? S\u225?u\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   LAI\u8217?s Coffee\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Sleeper bus to Ha Giang\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Monday \u8226? 10-12-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 18 in Vietnam. Day 4 in Da Nang. Day 1 in Hue. We woke up, headed downstairs to eat breakfast. Headed back to the room then got in our Grab to head to Hue. We stopped by a coffee shop to get salt coffee and talked with my Dad\u8217?s cousin. He owns the coffee shop and lives upstairs. We explored the shrine above his shop and lit some incense. We then left to go see Dad\u8217?s aunt however we went into the wrong house then found out that she wasn\u8217?t there. She had already left to Saigon. We mistaken the house and went next door to their actual house. We went in and talked for a bit. We left then headed to the Hue Imperial City. We explored all of the attractions in the mini city then headed out. We went back to my dad\u8217?s cousin\u8217?s cafe then went out to eat. We spoke for a bit and I found out that he used to be a bartender and used to own a nightclub. He used to deal w gangsters, prostitutes, and drug dealers. We walked to the restaurant, ate, then walked back to the coffee shop. We then drank some more coffee and talked for a bit before heading back to the hotel. I saw that they also owned two cats. We made our way back to the hotel where we also paid our driver for booking our flight, driving us around and acting as our personal assistant. I showered then went to sleep. 13.6k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Drive to Hue\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   An Coffee & Tea\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dad\u8217?s aunt\u8217?s house\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hue Imperial City\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hue Museum of Royal Antiquities\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Th\u225?i H\u242?a Palace\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   C\u224?n Th\u224?nh Hall\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Truong Sanh Palace\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   An Coffee & Tea\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Qu\u225?n B\u225?nh B\u232?o N\u7853?m L\u7885?c Hu\u7871? X\u432?a\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Sunday \u8226? 10-11-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 17 in Vietnam. Day 3 in Da Nang. Day 1 in Hoi An. Woke up and ate breakfast @ the breakfast buffet. We went back to the room to get ready then headed out to Hoi An. We stopped by a store that sold statues. I ended up buying a bracelet for $12. Then we headed to Hoi An. We did a boat tour I ended up buying pics for $4. We then headed to downtown Hoi An and stopped by a shoe store that our driver\u8217?s sister owned. We investigated but didn\u8217?t buy anything. We then walked around and I went into I Love Fashion. I bought three pairs of fitted Birkenstocks. We then headed out and took pics of a temple. We then walked around for a bit more and I bought some lanterns and a flying bird from a man on the street. We then stumbled into the Japanese bridge but to get in we had to pay for a ticket. We walked away and just kept window shopping. We took pics @ another temple we ran into then bought some custom made chopsticks. Instead of going to a restaurant, we stopped by to eat lunch @ a random lady\u8217?s food stall. We then sat @ a cafe and I had egg and salt coffee. We sat for a while relaxing before heading out and checking out several stores hiding from the sun. I bought a bunch of souvenirs then headed over to the assembly hall. They needed a ticket so I only took pics. We then walked around chatting w locals and buying souvenirs. Dad bought me a sugarcane juice. Then we headed over to a lantern boat tour. It was great, we took pics and enjoyed the ride. We got into our drivers car then headed back to the hotel. I also got a banh mi using grab. It was less than $3 so it was pretty cheap. 11.5k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Drive to Hoi An\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Statue shop\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Boat tour @\u272?\u7912?C VINH TR\u7846?N\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   I love fashion\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Ch\u249?a B\u224? M\u7909?\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Ch\u249?a C\u7847?u\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @random vendor\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Fujian Assembly Hall\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Market\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   I love fashion\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lantern boat tour\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner Banh Mi\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Saturday \u8226? 10-10-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 16 in Vietnam. Day 2 in Da Nang. Woke up and went downstairs to eat breakfast. We then waited for our Grab and when we went outside someone else backed their car into a pole. We got into the Grab then headed to Ba Na Hills. We bought tickets online then headed to the cable cars to go on a 25 min ride to the top. It wasn\u8217?t as expected since it was rainy. I would come here next time if it wasn\u8217?t raining. We took shelter in an indoor amusement park where we watched a dancing performance, bumber cars, 5D theater, 4D theater, drop tower ride, then we went to go eat at the buffet. We then went to go get a free pastry and beer. We each got a free pastry however whenever we were trying to get a free beer they said we could only get one or the other. But the guy working the bar gave us 3 free beers. We then sat and relaxed for a bit before heading out to the Golden Bridge. Took some mid pics since it was foggy but still quite the experience. We started heading towards a Buddhist temple and dad made friends w this one lady w her daughter. They started talking a lot and we eventually merged our groups together. We sat and talked for a bit next to the Buddha temple and we went out to eat w them. We had to wait for their other daughter who worked at the park to clock off of work before heading out to eat. We didn\u8217?t go home using our driver, we actually car pooled w the new family we met and ended up eating and talking w them. We ate bun bo hue and then went got a grab back to the hotel. We got home, I spoke w the receptionist for a bit then went went back to the room, showered then went to sleep. 15.4k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Ba Na Hills\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Friday \u8226? 10-9-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 15 in Vietnam. Day 1 in Da Nang. We arrived in Da Nang @5:30am. Checked into the hotel then walked to eat breakfast @Suat An Van Phong. We got an egg coffee next door. We then went back to the hotel to shower then we walked outside to do laundry next door. We then walked into the laundry place and walked into dad\u8217?s uncle\u8217?s place. We greeted them and talked for a bit before heading out going on a walk. We walked around taking pics and we stopped by a library to check out the public libraries in VN. We sat for a bit @ Starbucks since dad wanted a coffee. We then headed to the Da Nang museum. I spent sometime in the museum learning ab the history of Da Nang. When I finished exploring, I found dad waiting in the lobby but we were looking for mom. We stayed for a bit looking for mom walking up and down the street but eventually walked back to the hotel. I played the piano for a bit then headed out to look for mom. Dad found me and mom was @ Dad\u8217?s uncle\u8217?s house. We headed out to eat lunch and I talked to dad\u8217?s uncle ab his experience in the war. He has good and bad memories. He was the captain of a ship w a 7 man crew and went to jail 3 times for trying to illegal cross the border. After lunch we went back to the hotel and took a nap. I woke up, then went out to walk around the area. We ran into a Buddhist temple but it was nothing special so we took pics then moved along. We circled back to the hotel and I parted ways w mom n dad. I ended up going to a park with nice architecture and public art sculptures. There were groups of young ppl dancing. Then I headed back to meet @Dad\u8217?s uncle\u8217?s house to have dinner. They had eggplant and it tasted better than I had expected. I also got a $100 tip from my first cousin once removed. They also had an orange cat tied. We then walked over to the bridge and it was ~30 mins just to get there. We used the restroom and paid 5000 dong per person which is a first for me. I got on the bridge early @8pm and stayed until 9pm. They also closed the road so I think I could\u8217?ve joined later and got a perfect spot. It was great. It sprayed Fire and Water and the water made it feel like a party. My mom also met a Vietnamese girl and we took shelter using her poncho. When her boyfriend came back he didn\u8217?t look pleased. It gave insecure. We got a grab back to the hotel, showered, then went to sleep. 21.0k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Arrived in Da Nang\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Breakfast @Suat An Van Phong\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Coffee @Kem Dua Ma Lai\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dad\u8217?s uncle\u8217?s house\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   \u272?\u224? N\u7861?ng Museum\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Dim Sum\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Ch\u249?a T\u226?n Ninh\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   APEC Park\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Dad\u8217?s uncle\u8217?s house\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dragon Bridge\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Thursday \u8226? 10-8-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 14 in Vietnam. Day 5 in Nha Trang. Woke up, packed a bit to get ready for Da Nang, went downstairs to eat breakfast, went back to the room to rest for a bit. I went to workout then headed back to the room. I showered, finished packing, then we checked out of the hotel @12pm. We met up w the driver and instead of driving us to Vincom Plaza he decided to take us to Go, a grocery store. We walked around for 40 mins then decided to go to Vincom Plaza. We walked around and bought stuff @ a grocery store called WinMart. I then ate lunch @Magic Chicken and I had a banh mi. We then went downstairs and I got a coffee @Phuc Long. We stayed for a couple of hours playing chess, clash of clans and being on my phone until we finally walked back to the hotel. We waited until we got picked up by our driver and he dropped us off where we bought our bus ticket. I also tipped our driver $20 since he was nice to us during our trip. We then took a sprinter van to a bus station. We then got into a sleeper bus then headed over to Da Nang. 10.5k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pack for Da Nang\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Check out of hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   GO! Nha Trang\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Vincom Plaza Tr\u7847?n Ph\u250?\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Magic Chicken\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Coffee @Ph\u250?c Long Vincom Tr\u7847?n Ph\u250? Nha Trang\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Sleeper bus to Da Nang\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Wednesday \u8226? 10-7-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 13 in Vietnam. Day 4 in Nha Trang. Woke up, went to go eat breakfast downstairs. Then headed back up to the room to brush my teeth and get ready for the day. We headed out to start our adventure. We started by going w our Grab driver we drove w two days ago to buy tickets to a sleeper bus to Da Nang. We then headed to our first attraction called H\u242?n Ch\u7891?ng. We then stopped by a sugarcane drink stall on the side of the road. We then headed to take a pic of CAFE \u272?\u211?. We couldn\u8217?t go inside but we stayed in the area to take pics. We then headed to Ba L\u224?ng Church. We got inside of the church and took pics inside as well. We then headed to the Museum of Oceanography. We toured the museum then headed to get lunch @ a seafood restaurant. We headed back to the hotel and took a nap. Our driver had family issues so he had to go home early. I woke up from my nap then went downstairs to grab a coffee. I got a a milk iced coffee. I got tired of waiting for my parents so I just went to go walk around Gold Coast Mall Nha Trang which was a mall around the corner. I went back to the room to find both of my parents there mad at each other. So I went to eat dinner @McDonalds and tried communicating w the worker there. I ran into dad in the lobby and used the restroom then waited for him. Wait for 15 mins before heading out w mom walking around shopping. Ended up buying stuff for mom and some more pins. Went back to the hotel, showered, then went to sleep. 17.2k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   H\u242?n Ch\u7891?ng\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   CAFE \u272?\u211?\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Ba L\u224?ng Church\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Museum of Oceanography\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Vua Hai San Gia Re\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Coffee @Ph\u250?c Long\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Gold Coast Mall Nha Trang\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @McDonalds\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   S\u7840?P Souvenirs\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Night Market Nha Trang Ch\u7907? \u272?\u234?m Nha Trang\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Tuesday \u8226? 10-6-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 12 in Vietnam. Day 3 in Nha Trang. Woke up ~5:50am. Went to eat breakfast then headed out to go on our first excursion of the day. We got in the van and headed to the boat to take us to the island called H\u242?n Mi\u7877?u. We got on the speedboat and the views were amazing. We got to a floating waiting area and got lucky since we were the first ones there so there was no wait. I scuba dive for the first time for $40 and got a vid for an extra $12. I didn\u8217?t have to swim since they were carrying me around so I didn\u8217?t get flippers. When I first got in the little fish were nibbling my hands and feet. It tickled but it was my first time fish interacted with me willingly. I also touched anemones for the first time. I didn\u8217?t think I was allowed to but my diving partner touched it first. We got up, got my video then posted on insta. The boat showed up then we arrived to a resort. I bought some fried chicken to snack on before eating lunch. I walked around taking pics of sculptures then ran into the mud bath area and the mineral pools. I swam for a bit but it was quite shallow in the area I went into. I was looking for salt coffee but ended up not finding any. I used the restroom and ran into a naked Asian man. Scary. I then walked around and found my way to the beach where my parents were relaxing at. I then went to try parasailing for the first time. I got on a jet ski to get to a different side of the island to do parasailing for 1.5km. It was a total of $64 for 1.5km and a video recording. It was amazing however parasailing also hurt the inside of my legs. We relaxed for a bit on the beach then we went to go get food at a floating restaurant. It was the first time at a wet restaurant like this and they made the food fresh. After we ate I took a 20 min nap on a hammock. I woke up then we headed back on the boat to get to the mainland. We got a grab then headed back to the hotel. I went to go workout and used the steam room again. I went back to the room, showered, and relaxed in bed for a bit. Mom went to dad\u8217?s friends room since she was by herself and me and dad went to go get Texas Chicken. We ate in their hotel room. Apparently Dad\u8217?s friend and his gf are having issues. He went to his friend\u8217?s house to eat and left his gf at the hotel we ended up eating fried chicken w her and invited her out but she didn\u8217?t want to come. We then went downstairs and checked out the casino. There were only digital table games and it was quite small w a lot of slots. We left to go walk by the beach and got the tea that his friend has been a spoiled brat since a young age and says he is smarter than his friend and he got lucky bc he was born into a family in business. We arrived @Tram Huong Tower then walked over to the night market. I bought some more souvenirs then headed back to the hotel. We stopped by Starbucks to use the restroom then made our way back to the hotel. We checked out the first floor of the mall in the hotel then went back to the room. I showered, sorted my souvenirs, then went to sleep. 13.5k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Scuba diving\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Parasailing\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @B\u232? Tu\u7845?n H\u7841?nh\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Texas Chicken\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Tram Huong Tower\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Night Market Nha Trang\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Monday \u8226? 10-5-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 11 in Vietnam. Day 2 in Nha Trang. Woke up ~6am and we headed out to eat breakfast. I couldn\u8217?t find my parents so I went out to eat @Qu\u225?n N\u432?\u7899?ng Anh Tho\u7841?i which was a random com tam restaurant. It was originally 30k but for me it was 50k. I left then got a coffee with coconut milk. I sat outside for a bit and started ppl watching then headed back to the hotel since dad texted me to come back. I got to the hotel and went to the breakfast buffet on the 1st floor, not the ground level. We then went to a huge Buddha statue that my mom went to when she was 9 called Ph\u7853?t th\u237?ch ca.   We couldn\u8217?t go inside of the temple since I had shorts and a sleeveless shirt on so we went to another Buddhist temple our taxi driver for the day showed us. It had a golden tower and was by far the most expensive and newest temple we have been to. It was called Tr\u250?c L\u226?m Ph\u7909?ng Thu\u7923? S\u417?n, Nha Trang. We then went to a Cham Hindu Tower that now has Buddhism influences. Took pics then went to go eat @ a seafood restaurant where the seafood was fresh. Loved the snail. We then went to a day market called Dam Market Ch\u7907? \u272?\u7847?m. We walked around, I tried looking for a new Fanny pack and souvenirs but ended up leaving w a coconut coffee. We went back to the hotel and while my parents napped, I worked out. It was a great gym w everything I needed. There was a huge swimming pool, sauna room, and a steam room as well. It was my first time using a steam room and I think I prefer the steam room. I went upstairs to shower then we went straight to the beach. I didn\u8217?t get into the water. I just enjoyed the weather, deleting photos, and sorting photos. I almost had to pay $4 for sitting on a chair but I ended up moving to the chairs we already paid for. We went back to the hotel and while mom got ready I did some shopping and finished exploring the Nha Trang Center. I bought a bear souvenir for $7 then headed out to eat bun bo hue @ my dad\u8217?s friend\u8217?s house. We walked home and otw back I stopped by a souvenir store and bought a pin. Then we arrived @ the hotel. We got to the room, showered, then went to sleep. 18.1k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Breakfast @Qu\u225?n N\u432?\u7899?ng Anh Tho\u7841?i\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Coffee @KATINAT COFFEE & TEA HOUSE\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Ph\u7853?t th\u237?ch ca\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Tr\u250?c L\u226?m Ph\u7909?ng Thu\u7923? S\u417?n, Nha Trang\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Po Nagar Temple\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Qu\u225?n H\u7843?i S\u7843?n B\u7901? K\u232? X\u243?m C\u7891?n 79\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dam Market Ch\u7907? \u272?\u7847?m\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Beach\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nha Trang Center\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Dad\u8217?s friend\u8217?s house\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Sunday \u8226? 10-4-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 10 in Vietnam. Day 4 in Binh Hoa. Day 1 in Nha Trang. Woke up ~6:40am then packed up our stuff then headed out to eat breakfast. Dad got me a salt coffee then went to go to get coffee in search of egg coffee @Trung Nguyen. We met and talked w the owner. We took a pic and my dad got his number whenever he comes to Houston. We then left and got into the van to head to Nha Trang. We stopped by my dad\u8217?s friend\u8217?s house and his hammock cafe. We got a coconut water, talked for a bit then headed back on the road. We stopped by a restaurant to have lunch called Nh\u224? h\u224?ng - Nh\u224? ngh\u7881? Bi\u7875?n V\u297?nh H\u7843?o. We got back on the road and finally got to the hotel @6:30pm. We checked into our rooms, rested for a bit, then headed out to eat dinner and had b\u250?n c\u225? for the first time. We then headed to Brian\u8217?s friends house where he met w his old friend and I talked with him as well. Otw back to the hotel, we heard live music and was drawn in. We got a beer and enjoyed the live music while I took pics for me and the family. We headed back to the hotel and I decided to walk the Nha Trang Center while the parents sat and talked for a bit. I window shopped and talked to some locals before heading up to the room when the mall closed @10pm. Showered then went to sleep. 11.0k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Breakfast @B\u225?nh Canh Anh B\u233?o\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Coffee @Trung Nguy\u234?n E-Coffee\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Head to Nha Trang\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Ca Phe Vong\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Nh\u224? h\u224?ng - Nh\u224? ngh\u7881? Bi\u7875?n V\u297?nh H\u7843?o\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @B\u250?n C\u225? Nguy\u234?n Loan\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dad\u8217?s friend\u8217?s friend\u8217?s house\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Beer @Nh\u224? H\u224?ng Palms Bistro Nhatrang\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nha Trang Center\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Saturday \u8226? 10-3-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 9 in Vietnam. Day 3 in Binh Hoa. Woke up ~5am. Went out to eat breakfast @ a random hole in the wall restaurant called H\u7911? T\u237?u H\u224?i C\u7889?t. Went back to the house, rested, then headed out to walk to a local market. I got a salt coffee at a random stall then we headed back to the house. We then went out to my grandpa\u8217?s brother\u8217?s house. We talked for a bit, walked w dad down the street for a bit and getting a drink, then getting in the car to visit mom\u8217?s old house. We then went to go get lunch at a restaurant where I got another salt coffee. We sat there for a while, lo no enough where I got bored. We finally left on our 1 he commute to head back to the house. We showered then rested for ~15 mins then headed to my cousin\u8217?s house. They had the nicest house I\u8217?ve been to so far. To understand how they are related to me took a while. Basically my uncle in law has a daughter, who is my cousin in law. My mom has a sister who married a man. This man has a brother who has a daughter. We went to the daughter\u8217?s house, which is technically my cousin in law. We talked, ate, drank, and I played the piano. It was a great time but we went home. 8.3k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Breakfast @H\u7911? T\u237?u H\u224?i C\u7889?t\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Great uncle\u8217?s house (mom\u8217?s side)\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Mom\u8217?s old house\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Quan T\u237?\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Mom\u8217?s sister\u8217?s house\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   My cousin\u8217?s house (by marriage)\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Friday \u8226? 10-2-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 8 in Vietnam. Day 2 in Binh Hoa. Woke up ~5am, then headed out to walk around the area. I got yellow rice @ a random woman\u8217?s stall. Then I got coffee @Thang Binh Cafe. It was a milk coffee so it was kinda bitter. I prefer salt coffee. Dad ate a banh mi while I ate my food. We watched some chu\u8217?s playing Chinese chess in their natural habitat. We went back to the house to rest for a bit and use the restroom while we waited for Tung to come pick us up w his car. We waited w some other Chu\u8217?s dad befriended then we went to a temple where students were studying. We took pics then headed to an amusement park that seemed a bit abandoned. It was a nice, quiet, and peaceful get away from the city. We then ate lunch and it was great. We had snail, beef, pork, fish, dumplings, drinks all for a great price. We then went to my cousin\u8217?s house and it was probably the best Vietnamese house I\u8217?ve seen so far. The interior was aesthetic with light brown, white, and black colors. We talked and did a house tour, then went headed to another Buddhist temple which was quite small. Then we headed to another Buddhist temple which was by far the best temple we\u8217?ve been to. We took pics and saw monkeys. We then headed back to mom\u8217?s aunts house to pick up some gifts for dad\u8217?s teacher. We headed to dad\u8217?s teacher\u8217?s house to give them a visit. We talked for a bit then headed out to eat some balut. I had 4  then we went to get some coffee. We went back to their house and I practiced piano and learned a new part of Fugue in G. We relaxed for a bit then headed home.  14.3k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Coffee @Thang Binh Cafe\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Tran Bien Temple of Literature\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Buu Long Tourist Area\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @LONG WANG K33 V\u245? Th\u7883? S\u225?u, Ph\u432?\u7901?ng Tr\u7845?n Bi\u234?n, TP \u272?\u7891?ng Nai\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Cousin\u8217?s house\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dai Giac Ancient Buddhist Temple\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Chau Thoi Buddhist Temple\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Mom\u8217?s Sister\u8217?s house\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dad\u8217?s Teacher\u8217?s house\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Qu\u225?n H\u7897?t V\u7883?t L\u7897?n Thu H\u224?\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Highlands Coffee\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Mom\u8217?s Sister\u8217?s house\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Thursday \u8226? 10-1-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 7 in Vietnam. Day 7 in Ho Chi Minh City. Day 1 in Binh Hoa. Woke up ~6am. Ate breakfast at the buffet, then went back to the hotel room to start packing so we can go to Binh Hoa. I showered then rested for a bit before heading over to dad\u8217?s friend\u8217?s house. The grab ride had a manual so it was a bumpy ride. We arrived then went to eat broken rice @C\u417?m t\u7845?m ch\u225?o \u7871?ch again. It was great then we got salt coffee w coconut @MUSEUM Coffee. We sat in the coffee shop and drank 2 coffees and talked to dad\u8217?s friend. I learned a lot of Vietnamese and I eventually learned \u8220?mom gap lie\u8221? as a goodbye. We went back to his house to wait for dad. Dad arrived then we headed to Binh Hoa to mom\u8217?s sister\u8217?s house. We arrived and we ate and talked for a bit before taking a shower. 3.3k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pay rent\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Applied for unemployment\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @C\u417?m t\u7845?m ch\u225?o \u7871?ch\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Coffee @MUSEUM Coffee\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Mom\u8217?s sister\u8217?s house\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Wednesday \u8226? 9-30-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 6 in Vietnam. Day 6 in Ho Chi Minh City. Woke up ~5am. Ate breakfast at the buffet then went back to the room to rest for a bit since it started raining hard. We then headed out to get a full body massage @Massage C\u7893? Phong Q3 | G\u7897?i \u272?\u7847?u D\u432?\u7905?ng Sinh. It took us ~4 hours from 10am to 2pm to finish the massage. They gave us herbal tea and a soup after our massage. We went back get some food @ a Cantonese restaurant then headed back to the hotel to get ready for dinner. We rested for ~30 mins then got a grab to dad\u8217?s friend\u8217?s girlfriend\u8217?s place and it was 1.5 hours to get there, so I took a nap. We got there around 5pm and my leg was asleep whenever I stepped out of the car. We then ate food and my favorite was the snail. It was a pretty nice house and the bathroom was outside with no sink or mirror in the bathroom. I sat with the male adults and ate and drank beer w them. This was the first time drinking w the chus and it was an experience. They were all friendly making sure I ate and there was this one guy saying I was OK. He was praising me for wanting to learn and sitting at the table. Other people aren\u8217?t like that and aren\u8217?t willing to learn, so I\u8217?m \u8220?OK\u8221?. We headed home and I took a nap otw back. We got home ~11pm, I showered and went to sleep. 1.7k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Massage @Massage C\u7893? Phong Q3 | G\u7897?i \u272?\u7847?u D\u432?\u7905?ng Sinh\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Song Restaurant\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Dad\u8217?s friend\u8217?s girlfriend\u8217?s house\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Tuesday \u8226? 9-29-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 5 in Vietnam. Day 5 in Ho Chi Minh City. Woke up around 6am and then went to go eat breakfast. We got a grab and headed over to Oasis Cafe and it blew my expectations. It was colorful and wasn\u8217?t as busy as expected. We got drinks and fish food so we fed the fish before my dad gave it away to some kid. L father. We walked around and took vids/pics and then headed out to our first store of the day. Stopped by a streetwear store that was three stories high and I ended up buying 2 jackets and 1 jort. We headed to another store but it only had 1 floor so we left pretty quickly. We then headed to go get some lunch @B\u225?nh X\u232?o 46A. We ate banh xeo and we spoke w an American named Eli. He was from Minnesota and was here on vacation. My parents went to go get ready for their dentist appointment so I got some free time by myself. I went to T\u226?n \u272?\u7883?nh Market but it wasn\u8217?t as good as I thought. Seemed more local with less souvenirs. Then I headed over to a Buddhist temple. Saw a cat and took some pics before heading across the street to a historical landmark and taking pics. I then walked over to a popular cafe and got a salted coffee and relaxed for a bit in the ac. I took pics/vids and saw a cat on the way out. I then took a grab for the first time to a template. The guy was friendly and was 26 years old and said he was the best driver in the city. I walked around and used the restroom since they didn\u8217?t allow pics in the main hall. I then walked to the HCMC museum and took pics before heading out. I took a grab to go see Saigon Swagger but didn\u8217?t find anything I liked. I started walking to the Saigon Centre however Ben Thanh market was otw so I stopped there to do some more shopping. I bought some more souvenirs then I got a text to go back to the hotel. I got back and we went out to eat chow. We ate chow then balut after. We then started walking and made our way to Bui Vien street. It was overstimulating but I would go again. We got a grab back to the hotel and I showered and went to sleep. 21.3k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Oasis Cafe\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Whose Studio\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Sly\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @B\u225?nh X\u232?o 46A\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nh\u224? Th\u7901? Gi\u225?o X\u7913? T\u226?n \u272?\u7883?nh\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   T\u226?n \u272?\u7883?nh Market\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Vinh Nghiem Buddhist Temple\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Bia t\u432?\u7903?ng ni\u7879?m\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Ng\u226?m Coffee\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Jade Emperor Pagoda\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   HCMC History Museum\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   SAIGONSWAGGER - 26 L\u253? T\u7921? Tr\u7885?ng\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Ben Thanh Market\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @C\u7853?u Ch\u225?o\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Bui Vien Street\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Monday \u8226? 9-28-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 4 in Vietnam. Day 4 in Ho Chi Minh City. Woke up early ~5:30am and watched YouTube before heading out to eat @ the breakfast buffet. Drank some coffee while talking to Val on ft then got ready for the Cu Chi Tunnel tour. They picked us up and we headed to the tunnels. We stopped by a handcrafting place where they made art work with oils and egg shells. We donated $4 then headed back on the road. We went on the tour and learned about the traps, tunnels, the way the Vietnamese lived in the tunnels, and their perspective. There was a little girl who killed multiple American soldiers and they called her a war hero. We then got dropped off at the hotel and dad wasn\u8217?t there so we just walked around looking for a food spot. We found a new restaurant w a bunch of young ppl so me and Mom stopped to eat some lunch @B\u225?nh \u431?\u7899?t Ban M\u234? Giang V\u432?\u417?ng - T\u244?n Th\u7845?t T\u249?ng. We tried new foods and I thought it was great. We then headed back to the hotel to look for dad and on the way back we stopped at a tourist tour location looking for excursions to do. We then headed back to the hotel to find dad and end up not finding him. We stopped by the tourist tour location bc mom left her glasses case on the table so we stopped by and picked up her glasses case. We went on our own adventure and walked to a Hindu Temple. I took pics, then dad texted, and we met up at the hotel. Dad was hungry so we went to get a banh mi @B\u225?nh M\u236? Huynh Hoa - L\u234? Th\u7883? Ri\u234?ng. We then headed back to the hotel so dad could eat and we rest before going out to Bui Vien street. We ended up taking a nap @7:10pm, then I woke up @10:30pm. So I just went to sleep. 10.2k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Cu Chi Tunnels\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @B\u225?nh \u431?\u7899?t Ban M\u234? Giang V\u432?\u417?ng - T\u244?n Th\u7845?t T\u249?ng\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Ann Tours Co\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Mariamman Hindu temple\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   B\u225?nh M\u236? Huynh Hoa - L\u234? Th\u7883? Ri\u234?ng\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Saturday \u8226? 9-26-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 2 in Vietnam. Day 2 in Ho Chi Minh City. Woke up @3am due to jet lag. So we went out to walk around and stopped by a Pho restaurant to eat. We then walked around sight seeing and stopped by a Catholic Church. Saw some rats, dogs, and a couple of homeless people. This reminds me a lot of New York. We went back to the hotel to rest for a bit, then we went to eat the breakfast buffet at the hotel. We ate, then headed out to do some shopping @Ben Thanh Market. Bought some shirts, snow globe, and some capybaras keychains. After shopping, we headed to another market Dad wanted to go to called Pham Van Hai Market. Parents did some shopping around for some clothes and me and mom tried Che. I saw a short old Asian women selling toothpicks for 40 cents, which was sad to see. She was about 70-80 years old. We then kept walking and headed to the meat area of the market then got some sugar cane juice at a random stall that dad used to go to. We then headed to Dad\u8217?s friend\u8217?s house where we chatted in his home. I like how the garage is built into his living room. The garage opens up to the living room. We then headed to a coffee shop and I tried salt coffee for the first time @Trung Nguy\u234?n Legend where I also bought souvenirs for the Louis neighbors. We headed back to Dad\u8217?s friend\u8217?s place where we dropped off our souvenirs then went out again to get some Com Tam (broken rice) and it was nice and spicy. We then headed to Dad\u8217?s dentist appointment and I ended up getting a teeth cleaning @Nha khoa Lan Anh. It started raining on us so we took shelter inside of a store and waited for our Grab ride. We then headed to eat dinner at another pho spot. We got a grab back to the hotel. I showered, sorted my souvenirs, and got ready for bed. Went to sleep early today @7:30pm. 12.8k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Breakfast @Pho Vietnam\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nh\u224? th\u7901? Huy\u7879?n S\u7929?\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Ben Thanh Market\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pham Van Hai Market\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Trung Nguy\u234?n Legend\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @C\u417?m t\u7845?m ch\u225?o \u7871?ch\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nha khoa Lan Anh\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Pho Nam Huong\par \li0\fi0 \par \li0\fi0 Sundaey \u8226? 9-27-2026\par \li0\fi0 Day 3 in Vietnam. Day 3 in Ho Chi Minh City. Woke up around 5am today. Got dressed then went to eat at the buffet. We headed to the Saigon Ventral post office and walked around looking at souvenirs. Me and mom booked a trip to Cu Chi Tunnels for tomorrow morning. We then headed over to the Notre Dame Cathedral but the front had scaffolds in front so I couldn\u8217?t get a pic. We got in after lying to the security that we were religious so when we left the guy confronted us. We then walked over the Saigon Book Street, took pics and bought a coffee @Highlands Coffee. We were about to leave then we saw some kids getting ready for a dragon dance performance. We stayed and watched them dance. They even came up to me and I poked the kid\u8217?s stomach. We then headed over to the Independence Palace and toured the building. We then headed to get some food @C\u417?m Ni\u234?u S\u224?i G\u242?n. We then walked to the War Remnants Museum of the Vietnam war and it was quite the experience. Dad didn\u8217?t want to go in because he disagrees with their pov however it portrays the US as the war aggressor and how we killed innocent civilians during our time in the Vietnam war. They made comments like \u8220?the Vietnamese people were the US playground for military use. Their military experiments were used on living targets for US experience. After exploring the museum with mom, we found dad talking with two Australians about their political beliefs. We talked for ~30 mins before heading out. We then walked back to the hotel walking through a park on the way back. There were kids outside playing and an outdoor gym which I thought was pretty cool. Went back to the hotel, showered, then got ready to go eat dinner w Dad and Quang\u8217?s mom\u8217?s friend. We ate @ then they drove us around the city showing us the lights, driving over the bridge and under the river. We were falling asleep so we went home, I showered, then went to sleep. 13.6k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Saigon Central Post Office\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Notre Dame Cathedral of Saigon\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Saigon Book Street\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Highlands Coffee\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Independence Palace\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @C\u417?m Ni\u234?u S\u224?i G\u242?n\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   War Remnants Museum\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Wednesday \u8226? 9-23-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up @5am to go to Houston, got gas and made it home safe. Ended up relaxing, playing games and eating all day. Headed to the airport and headed to Vietnam.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Drove to Houston\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Gas\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Flight to Taiwan\par \li0\fi0 \par \li0\fi0 Thursday/Friday \u8226? 9-24-2026/9-25-2026\par \li0\fi0 Day 1 in Vietnam. Day 1 in Ho Chi Minh City. On the 15 hour flight, I slept and watched One Day, Michael, and started Backrooms. Got to an airport in Taiwan and I loved the airport. Walked around taking pictures and played on a public piano I saw. Got on the next flight to Vietnam, finished Backrooms, and started Ready Player One. Made it to the hotel in a Grab and it was the first experience driving in Vietnam. Craziness everywhere, lots of honking and scooters. We got to the hotel and dropped off our luggage. I had dad\u8217?s friend\u8217?s toiletry bag in my luggage and the code for one of the latches got set somehow so we had to break it. We then went to get a shampoo and head massage. When we left it started raining so I made my way back to the apartment and took a shower and napped. I woke up to my parents in the room, got dressed then headed out to eat. Had Italian food instead of Vietnamese food but it was still good. We then walked around and did some window shopping before heading back to the hotel. Showered and went to sleep. 9.8k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Flight to Vietnam\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Shampoo & head massage @\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @M-Spirito Restaurant & Bar\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Tuesday \u8226? 9-22-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Washed dishes, fed the cats, did litter, made coffee, watched YouTube in the living room while drinking my coffee. Relaxing day. Worked out, then stopped by Tropical Smoothie Cafe to get a free smoothie with an a\u231?a\u237? bowl. Went to get some free tacos at Louis, but they ran out so I only had chips and dip, went home, started packing for Vietnam, ate a small dinner, then went on an evening walk with Gabe, Marianne, Mounika, and Mounika\u8217?s friend. Went home and finished packing, made dinner, ate, then went to sleep.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Smoothie @Tropical Smoothie Cafe\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Tacos @Louis\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Packed for Vietnam\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Evening walk\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Monday \u8226? 9-21-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Had a slow morning, Val made us breakfast, then we headed to Steven\u8217?s to drop him off at the airport. We went to HEB after and rested before going to the gym. We celebrated our first date anniversary by going to Pho MC and getting wonton pho for the first time.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dropped Steven off @airport\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   HEB\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Pho MC\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Sunday \u8226? 9-20-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up early for the Plano Balloon Festival and they didn\u8217?t fly any balloons because there was too much wind. We just got freebies and walked around. We went to Hmart to get rice and then went to a car meet @Ford\u8217?s Garage. We drove home, made food, ate, did litter, fed the cats, then took a nap while watching Love on the Spectrum, went to the gym, got home, made food, ate, washed dishes, fed the cats, then went to sleep.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Plano Balloon Festival\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hmart\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Car meet @Ford\u8217?s Garage\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Saturday \u8226? 9-19-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Made and ate breakfast, and me and Val did chores this morning. Washed dishes, threw away trash, vacuumed, litter, and I watched Vietnamese dishes on YouTube while Val setup her dream catcher.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Steven picked up the cats\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Picked up and dropped off Val\u8217?s sister to J Cole concert\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   HEB\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Jollibee\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Friday \u8226? 9-18-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Made Val's yogurt, fed the cats, made and ate breakfast, did the litter, went to go get coffee and pastries at the front office, washed dishes, vacummed, rearranged the living room, played chess and relaxed for a while, worked on the website, went to the gym to play basketball for 2+ hours, then met up with Val to eat @5 guys, went home, showered, fed the cats, did litter, then went to sleep.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Working on couple\u8217?s website\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @5 Guys\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Thursday \u8226? 9-17-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Fed the cats, did the litter, worked out, went to Costco to get protein powder, went home, showered, ate lunch while we watched Love on the Spectrum, Val took a nap while I doom scrolled, she woke up then we made dinner, watched Love on the Spectrum while we ate. We relaxed for the rest of the night. Slow day but relaxing.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Applied for unemployment\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Costco\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Wednesday \u8226? 9-16-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Fed the cats, ate some toast, went to the gym, got home, washed the dishes, made some brunch, fed the cats, helped Val make her yogurt, went to Cris Worley Fine Arts Museum which only took about 10 mins to view all of the galleries. Drove over to the Parr Park Rock Trail. I ended up going on the wrong path at first, but eventually found my way to the rock path. Stopped by a shawarma place to eat a lunch, went home, took a nap, went to Starbucks to get Winston and Moab pup cups, then went to have dinner @Gabe's and Marianne's. We were celebrating Winston's birthday and took pictures. I had Jollibee for the first time and it was good. The spaghetti was great and I would get food there again. We watched Love on the Spectrum and we will be starting this show. Kiki also pooped on Val.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Cris Worley Fine Arts Museum\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Parr Park Rock Trail\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @DFW Kabab & Gyro\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pupcups @Starbucks\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Gabe & Marianne's\par \li0\fi0 \par \li0\fi0 \par \b Tuesday \u8226? 9-15-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 1 of having 4 cats. Kiki is very territorial now. She hisses at everyone and Kumo seems to be the only one to stand up against her. Obama threw up his breakfast, Bean didn\u8217?t finish his food initially like he used to, Kumo has also changed his personality by not being as friendly. He seems to be more skittish. Bean runs away from Kiki a lot. Went with Gabe and Marianne to get some free bundt cakes @Nothing Bundt Cakes then went to the Galleria to buy some charms @Uniqlo. Got a smoothie from Thirsty's then bought some more souviners from Dallas and walked around the mall. Went home and got gas on the way back. We relaxed, took a 15 min nap then went to go walk on the Katy Trail. We went a bit too late for my liking so we would have to get there earlier ~6:30pm. Fed the cats, made food, showered, then went to sleep.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nothing Bundt Cakes\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Galleria\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Smoothie @Thirsty\u8217?s\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Gas\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Katy Trail\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Monday \u8226? 9-14-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Fed the cats, made breakfast, washed the dishes, cleaned litter, updated my personal website, then started working on Me and Val\u8217?s couples website. I have an idea of how I want it to look and I am starting from scratch. I used up all of my Claude request for the day so I\u8217?ll pick it up for tomorrow. Fed the cats, called Steve for the job position however he didn\u8217?t answer but I left a voicemail. We went to go pick up Kumo n Kiki @Steven\u8217?s and talked to him about his date. We went home and went on a walk with Mounika and talked about the moon and AI development.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Updated personal website\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Planned a couple\u8217?s website\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Picked up Kumo and Kiki @Steven\u8217?s\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Evening walk\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Sunday \u8226? 9-13-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Fed the cats, did the litter, made breakfast, washed dishes, replaced the trash. Then I started building my personal website. I\u8217?ve been