11?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Phone call w Steve\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Pho One w Kichang\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pool party @Manish\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Whataburger\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Thursday \u8226? 9-10-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Made breakfast, got dressed then went to return an Amazon package and pick up some packages @Whole Foods. Then hit Costco to get some groceries. Bought a caramel coffee frappe but I wouldn\u8217?t get it again. Headed to HEB to get more groceries then headed home. Had to call Gabe to open the door for us since the keys aren\u8217?t working. Picked up a package from the mailbox and set up the cat bed on the window. Worked out, went home, ate leftovers, went on an evening walk with Mounika, Gabe, and Marianne, showered,\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Whole Foods\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Costco\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   HEB\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Evening walk\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Wednesday \u8226? 9-9-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Ate toast as a snack, went to the gym and there was there horrible accident that caused an extra 15 min on our commute to the gym. It was a huge 18 wheeler that flipped over on its side. We then worked out, went home, fed the cats, made and ate a late breakfast, napped, did some chores cleaning around the house, then went to La Pasha to eat catch up with Rajiv. Went home, showered and went to sleep.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @La Pasha\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Tuesday \u8226? 9-8-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Made and ate breakfast, picked up the mailbox keys, and found my Amazon packages. I will return one but keep the other fan. Updated my budget from what others have sent me. Did some research into becoming a nurse. Did some planning on getting my next CS job by making a list of companies I want to work at and a list of topics I need to study. Val got home and vented on a bald black man stealing her parking spot. Went to the gym and decided not to workout and walk the Katy Trail instead. The trail was great and we are going to walk the trail whenever we have time. We went home, showered, cooked, watched Suits while we ate, then went to sleep.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Picked up mail keys\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Journaled\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Katy Trail\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Monday \u8226? 9-7-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Happy Labor Day! Fed the cats, ate breakfast, gave myself a haircut trim, planned on what to buy today since today is Labor Day. Watched a documentary on WW1 and the countries involved. Basically Austria Hungry started the war, Germany joined to attack Russia since it was inevitable, Germany was powerful but lost due to resources, and there were about 9.5 million people who died. Washed dishes, got groceries @HEB, did some more research into WW2, made lunch, took a nap, made some toast for Val, went to the gym, worked out, went home, made dinner, ate dinner, washed dishes, stayed up a bit to bedrot, then went to sleep.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   HEB\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Sunday \u8226? 9-6-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Fed the cats, washed the dishes, calculated my net worth, then went to go get coffee with Manish and Dlin. We talked for a bit then me and David planned to go to Flying Fish to get the oyster deal. When I parked there, Dlin said that he needed to sell a dresser so I went to him to sell a dresser. Manish followed me and we ended up helping Dlin sell a dresser. We made the spontaneous decision to go swimming and planned a pool party for Saturday. We went to Manish\u8217?s place and I wore some extra swim shorts. I swam into a wall while trying to swim across the pool in one breath. We left after Dlin needed to sell another piece of furniture and then we went to Manish\u8217?s place, got dressed then I headed home. I got home, ate some chips and guac, then got ready for the gym. Hit abs, played basketball for about an hour then went home, showered, ate dinner, washed dishes, budgeted, then got ready for bed.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Coffee @White Rhino\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Swimming @Manish\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Gas\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Budget\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Saturday \u8226? 9-5-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Ate leftover breakfast for breakfast, prepped the thit kho for the potluck today, did research about the history of Hawaii, napped, then cooked the thit kho, waited for Manish and Mounika to get ready and headed to Mengrui\u8217?s house. We ate, drank, and talked a bunch. Thomas and Edison were harassing me and stole my watch at one point. We went home, showered and went to sleep\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Cooked\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Potluck @Mengrui\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Friday \u8226? 9-4-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Made breakfast, stayed in bed a little longer today catching up on sleep. Then went to get lunch with Dlin and David at a Korean restaurant and talked. I went home and clipped Obama\u8217?s nails then went to go pick up Val\u8217?s medicine, workout, then picked up pork belly and quail eggs to make thit kho for Mengrui\u8217?s pot luck. Went home, ate dinner, showered, cleaned the kitchen then went to sleep.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Golden Spoon\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Picked up Val\u8217?s medicine\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hmart\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Thursday \u8226? 9-3-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up and dropped of Bean at the animal shelter to get neutered, dropped off Val\u8217?s bag @HEB, headed home, made breakfast, watched the news while playing Wizard 101, napped, woke up, made lunch, washed dishes, then went to go pick up Bean from the animal shelter. He is offically our cat.  then picked up Bean at the animal shelter. When we got home we fed them then I went to the gym. It was cut short because Val, Gabe, Mounika and Marianne wanted to go on a walk @8. We went on a walk around the lake then went to Somi Somi to get a dessert. It was cheaper than I expected and I got the warm option which was nice. Gabe wanted 85 degrees but it was closed so we just talked at the table. We also ran into Raj\u8217?s old QA friend. We went home then made dinner and went to sleep.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dropped Bean off to surgery\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dropped off Val\u8217?s bag\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Picked up Bean at shelter\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Picked up Bean from the shelterWorkout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Evening walk\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dessert @SomiSomi\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Wednesday \u8226? 9-2-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Arrived in Dallas. Got home and went straight to sleep around 8am. Woke up to having to take the Kind Clinic call in bed @10:10am, then went back to sleep, woke up, started unpacking, clearing emails, paid rent, then started doing chores around the apartment cleaning, went to HEB to get groceries for the week, got home, put up the groceries, ate some sushi, then headed out to get some Popeyes for MD for taking care of our cats. We got home, cleaned litter box, made dinner, ate dinner. While we were eating dinner, Gabe and Mounika knocked on our door to see if we wanted to get some StarBucks. Since we were in the middle of eating we couldn\u8217?t so we passed and finished eating. I also got a call from Mother talking about Steve needing a part time worker to expand his work, still a lot of missing details but I will call/text him tomorrow about the details. We then cleaned dishes, folded more laundry, then went to sleep.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Unpack\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pay rent\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Laundry\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Applied for unemployment\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   HEB\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Picked up Popeyes\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Picked up the cats\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Tuesday \u8226? 9-1-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 8 in Hawaii. Day 6 in Oahu. Woke up, ate leftovers for breakfast, then headed out to do some last minute shopping. We went to EbiNomi to play the piano however they were closed @9am and opened @10am. We saw the owner of EbiNomi and talked to him for a bit. He says he leaves the piano locked because homeless people destroy the piano and asked if I played piano. He said there was a famous Japanese pianist who played about a year ago and is on their website. I\u8217?ll have to check that out. The owner was nice and I felt encouraged to support his business so I wanted to buy some food before leaving. We left to go buy some souvenirs. We bought some magnets and a shot glass then headed over to EviNomi to play the piano and get some finger food. We played the piano, recorded some videos, and bought some fried squid. There were a couple of people who applauded and recorded videos of me but good thing I didn\u8217?t know because I would\u8217?ve felt nervous. We went back to the hotel and showered, packed, then checked out of the hotel. We made a last minute decision to go skydiving. The feeling of skydiving finally hit whenever we got one the plane and it started moving. It was amazing. It hurt my ears and my legs were hurting from the harness. Not sure if this is something I\u8217?d do as a career. We then left to go fill up gas then parked at a grocery store to eat some leftovers. We headed to one last stop to see a tree. We took some pics then headed out. On the way out we saw a clan of ~5 cats and weasels. We tried feeding them leftover steak enchiladas but the weasels seemed to be more interested. There was one cat that was blind in one eye \u-10179?\u-9068? Val also hit the only cat who was interested in eating food in the head with a piece of enchilada. We dropped off the rental car then headed to turn on my check in bag then went to the terminal. Go on the flight then headed home to Dallas. On the flight I killed time by watching Jurassic World: Fallen Kingdom, and planning which pictures to post on IG.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Gift shop\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Played piano @EbiNomi\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Snack @EbiNomi\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Packed for Dallas\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Sky dive @GoJump\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Gas\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hitachi Tree\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dropped off rental\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Flight to Dallas\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Monday \u8226? 8-31-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 7 in Hawaii. Day 5 in Oahu. Woke up, got dressed, then headed out for our first hike. We took pictures and videos on the top of the pill box of both checkpoints and went into the top one. We then headed to Diamond Head State Monument and this was by far the most touristy trail with a line waiting for the top of the hike. We got to the second point but didn\u8217?t even bother for the highest point waiting in a line that could\u8217?ve taken 30 mins. We then got some food since we were hungry then went back to the hotel to nap. We then went to a waterfall and this was by far the muddiest hike of all of the hikes we have been on. We stayed for about an hour taking pictures and videos of the waterfall. There were also a group of young high schoolers next to us and they seemed like locals. Must be cool to hang out at a waterfall after school or during the summer time. We left to get Mexican food and it was my first time having a chimichanga. We then went back to the hotel to use the restroom and then headed out to chill at a beach. The first beach we attempted to go to was a fail since the vibes weren\u8217?t there. But the second beach was nice. The stars were out tonight and we listen to music and stargazed until Val fell asleep. We went back to the hotel and went to sleep. 18.0k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lanikai Pillbox Trail\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Diamond Head State Monument\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Thai Tacos\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lulumahu Falls\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Mexican Restaurant\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Kahala Beach\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Diamond Head Road Vista Point\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Sunday \u8226? 8-30-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 6 in Hawaii. Day 4 in Oahu. We woke up, got ready and headed out to the Pearl Harbor National Museum. We hit all of the museums and learned more about the history of Pearl Harbor. We ate at a food truck @Battleship Missouri Memorial because Val was getting a headache. She got a hamburger steak thinking it was a burger so I had to be a Karen to the workers and get her a burger. After the Pearl Harbor museums, we went to the local flea market and bought a capybara with a rice hat. We showed up a bit late so we just walked around a bit and window shopped. We left to eat Pho and it was a solid Pho spot. The restaurant was busy which was a great sign.we then went to a beach on the East side of the island. It was beautiful as always, great day outside, took a bit to find parking but found a spot and hit the beach. We just relaxed, walked the beach, took pictures, and chilled on our phones. We went back to the hotel, showered, then got dressed to walk around. We explored some shops and looked for a good spot until we ran into tacos. We went back to the hotel then ate them while watching Keeping Up with the Kardashians. 21.3k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   USS Arizona Memorial\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Battleship Missouri Memorial\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Sliders Grill\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pearl Harbor Aviation Museum\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pacific Fleet Submarine Museum\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Aloha Stadium Swap Meet\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch pt 2 @Stadium Pho\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lanikai Beach\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Surf n Turf Tacos\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Saturday \u8226? 8-29-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 5 in Hawaii. Day 3 in Oahu. Woke up, got ready then headed out for our first trail. Crouching lion had ropes out for assistance and was the most uneasy feeling trail due to the height of the view. We also got rained on so it made the trail extra slippery. We arrived to Turtle Beach and snorkeled there. The water was a bit murky and I didn\u8217?t see any turtles so we stayed there for ~30 mins. We hit up Turtle Beach and it was way better than Turtle Beach. It wasn\u8217?t a beach, but there were caves and a rocky terrain. We snorkeled here and got lucky enough to see a small sea turtle swimming in the wild. We went across the street to get some food and there were selling some clothes and had food trucks. We both got shrimp and a pineapple smoothie for lunch. Since we were in the north shore, we went to another food spot so that we didn\u8217?t have to come back to the north shore. Giovanni was packed and the food truck next to them were dead so they had about four open tables, so we tried to sit at one but they kicked us out. I\u8217?ll be giving them a 1 star on Google reviews. We then went to go get gas and ended up stopping by McDonalds to get some chicken nuggets and fries. After eating, we tried to go to Battery Barri but we needed base access in order to go to the memorial. We then headed back to the hotel to freshen up a bit. So we stopped by the ABC store and bought some laundry detergent and some dish soap so we could run laundry and hand wash my dirty shoes. While the laundry was running, we returned my Melin hat because I found my Uniqlo hat at the bottom of my backpack. We walked around and watched a show at the strip. It was bboys dancing and doing flips over people. It was cool but nothing tip worthy. After the clothes finished washing we headed back so we could run the dryer. We rested for 15 mins then headed back outside to walk the strip. Bought some magnets for me and Daniel then headed back to the hotel to sleep. 17.4k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Crouching Lion Trail\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Turtle Beach\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Shark\u8217?s Cove\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @North Shore Shrimp Truck\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pineapple smoothie @North Shore Tacos\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch pt 2 @Giovanni\u8217?s Shrimp Truck\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Gas\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch pt 3 @McDonalds\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Attempted to go to Battery Barri\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   ABC store\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Laundry\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Return Melin hat\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Gift shop\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Friday \u8226? 8-28-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 4 in Hawaii. Day 2 in Oahu. Woke up early then got dressed to go on our first hike. It was 1000+ steps to get to the summit and it was worth it. Going up was physically harder, but going down was mentally harder. We went back to the car and stopped by Val\u8217?s favorite beach and a blowhole. We then went on another hike to a viewpoint and see a light house. After the hike, we went to eat at a cafe and I had garlic shrimp and it was probably the best food I\u8217?ve had here. There were two pigeons who attack Val\u8217?s leftovers while I was playing my game and I had to fend for myself. We then drove back to the hotel and took a nap since the two hikes tired us out. We took a 2 hour nap then headed out to walk the strip. We stopped by all of the shopping centers and malls we encountered on the way and a lot of malls have greenery built into the mall. Bought some Thai Tea while we walked around. We stopped by a musubi cafe and I really enjoyed the musubi. I could see myself eating one a day for breakfast if I lived here. I think I lost my hat which bummed me out so I\u8217?m looking for another store to buy a hat at. I found a store called Melin and I liked the material and build of the hat. I might buy once since I think you could just throw them in the washer. After checking out another mall we went to the beach where we enjoyed the scenery, sorted photos and waited for fireworks @8pm. On the way out we saw a performer spinning fire on the beach. It was a 3 min show and it was our first street performer of the trip. We also saw a magician performing magic tricks. He blew me away with a trick where you say any card and the card shows up in the deck turned over. He also called on me and Val and he did an amazing job. He dealt with hecklers too smoothly. I spoke with him after the show by teaching me a trick. We went back to the hotel, showered, ate sandwiches, made sandwiches for tomorrow and went to sleep. 27k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Koko Head trail\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Halona Blowhole Lookout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Makapu\u8217?u Point Lighthouse Trailhead\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Kalapawai Cafe & Deli - Waimanalo\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   International Market Place\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Thai Tea @Uncle Sharkii Poke Bar\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Musubi Cafe Iyasume\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Royal Hawaiian Center\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Kahanamoku Beach\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Thursday \u8226? 8-27-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 3 in Hawaii. Day 3 in Kauai. Day 1 in Oahu. Woke up, ate Chicken in a Barrel leftovers for breakfast, got coffee, then headed out to Poipu Beach in hopes to find a sea turtle. We saw 3-4 goats on the way to the beach. We got to the beach and saw sea turtles immediately. We went snorkeling and saw fish, sea urchins, and sea slugs. There were sea lions lounging on the beach and another one was swimming around. We then checked out of the hotel and they were nice enough to allow us to leave at 11:10am instead of 11am. We then headed to a lighthouse in the area and saw a guy eating his food there on his lunch break. We talked to him for a bit and he said that he was from Cali living in his house his dad built in Hawaii and that he was a physical therapist. We then got an acai bowl @The Granola House, filled up gas which I think I put extra in the tank, then headed to drop off the car rental. It was my first car rental and first time driving a Camero but it was nice while it lasted. We took the shuttle to the airport then got to the terminal. I bought some airport food to save time on eating while waiting for our flight. We boarded the plane and I took a nap the whole flight. We then landed, picked up the checked luggage and then picked up our car rental. We\u8217?re driving a 2026 Mustang that gets an average of 15 miles per gallon. Rough. After we checked into the hotel, we then went to an Ala Moana Center which is a mall and we bought Thai Tea then walked around the mall buying souvenirs. It was a nice mall with its perks but not my favorite mall, nor I think is the best mall in Hawaii. We stopped by Walmart to get groceries for the week so we can make sandwiches. We went back to the hotel to drop off the groceries then got ready to go to a speakeasy called Wild Orange at HB Social Club. It was a nice cocktail lounge but we had fancy drinks and the most expensive caesar salad. After we left, we walked around the area and found ourselves at the end of a wrestling show. We went back to the hotel, showered, I made ramen noodles, then went to sleep. The hotel is a downgrade from our previous hotel in Kauai15.5k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Poipu Beach\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Checked out of hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Ninini Point Lighthouse\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   The Granola House\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Gas\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dropped off car rental\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @AI Ono Cafe\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Flight to Oahu\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Picked up car rental\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Checked into Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Ala Moana Center\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Thai tea @ShareTea\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   ABC store\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Walmart\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wild Orange at HB Social Club\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Wednesday \u8226? 8-26-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 2 in Hawaii. Day 2 in Kauai. Woke up naturally @5am and left the hotel bright and early before the sun came out. We began our 1 hour commute to the Waimea Canyon. We stopped by a coffee place in Hanapepe called Piling Coffee. We bought some coffee and a cinnamon roll. We started off the day by checking out the Red Dirt Waterfall. A unique experience and one of a kind landscape. I\u8217?ve never seen any red dirt naturally and for it to have a waterfall was an insane sight to see. We then headed to our first trail. We parked, paid for parking, then used the restroom before starting our first trail\u8212?Canyon Trail. It was about 3.3 miles round trip and we saw some amazing views along the way. A waterfall ended the hike and we put our feet into and water and took pics at the bottom. We explored above the waterfall and spent ~40 mins hanging out in the water. The trail to get to the top of the waterfall was probably the hardest trail of the day since there was a hint of danger along with the trail requiring using our hands for stability and not falling. On the way back to the car we saw a goat. We then headed to other look outs but on the way we stopped by Kokee Museum which also had a restaurant called Koke\u8217?s Lodge next to the museum so we stopped by and got some lunch. By this time we were quite hungry since we skipped breakfast so I had pulled pork, coleslaw, and sweet potatoes. We went to a couple more lookout, took pictures, then went on another trail\u8212?Pihea Trail. We didn\u8217?t finish this trail so we only walked about 1.3 miles round trip before heading to our next destination. We learned that the road system in Kauai isn\u8217?t an O, it\u8217?s more of a C. Since we were at the end of one side, to get to the other side took about 2 hours. So to get to Queen\u8217?s Bath, it took ~2 hours to get there. We just enjoyed the weather with the top down while listening to music. The Queen\u8217?s bath took me by surprise since there is a small trail to get to the Queen\u8217?s Bath. The trail was more slippery and a more technical trail and wearing slides didn\u8217?t help. We saw two sea turtles and took more pics while we were there. We headed to a grocery store in a plaza in hopes to find a restroom for Val\u8217?s however they were closed but there was a public restroom for us to use. There was this guy yelling at a girl on the phone saying \u8220?Who are you talking to bitch\u8221? and other verbal slurs towards her. We browsed some souvenirs in the gift shops and got drawn into the smell of BBQ nearby. We got some food @Chicken in a Barrel and got harassed by a chicken while eating. We then dropped the food into the car and bought some magnets at the gift shop. We saw a black cat outside, and while we were walking around it started to rain a bit. We ran to the car and started our commute home. We stopped by an ABC store and bought some more magnets. There was a Tran\u8217?s at the ABC store and it shocked me with their voice. We got home, showered and went to sleep. 20.6k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Coffee @Pilina Coffee\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Red Dirt Waterfall\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pu\u8217?u Hinahina lookout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Ni'ihau Viewpoint\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Canyon Trail\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Mini Falls\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Kokee Museum\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Koke\u8217?e Lodge\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pihea Trail\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Kalalau Lookout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pu\u8217?u O Kila Lookout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Queen\u8217?s Bath\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Chicken in a Barrel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Gift shop\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   ABC store\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Tuesday \u8226? 8-25-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 1 in Hawaii. Day 1 in Kauai. Woke up early @6am, made breakfast then headed to Val\u8217?s house for Mary to drop us off at the hotel. The flight from Dallas to Oahu was 7hrs and 45 mins. I tried my best to make the most of my time by watching new movies I\u8217?ve never watched. I watched The Devil Wears Prada 2 and Beetlejuice Beetlejuice. We shared some Panda Express and laid down while we waited for our flight from Oahu to Kauai. On the flight, we sat next to this older retired white man. He has a vacation home in Kauai and is married to a Vietnamese woman which I thought was awesome. Once we got to Kauai we went on a shuttle to go pick up our rental car. They offered a convertible car for the same price so now we are driving a convertible Camero for our time here in Kauai. We then checked into our hotel room and dropped off our luggage in our room, got dressed, then headed out. We went sight seeing in the area by driving around and taking pics. There are so many cats and chickens just roaming around. We stopped at a food truck to get dinner and ate it @Kapaa lookout which was nice with a convertible. We got tired and when to a local grocery store called Safeway to check it out but drove home after not buying anything. We got back to the hotel and explored around the hotel looking for the pools. We might check again during the daytime. We got back to the hotel room, showered, got settled and went to sleep. 9.5k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Flight to Oahu\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Panda Express\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Flight to Kauai\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Picked up rental car\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Checked into Hotel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wailua Falls\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Opaeka\u8217?a Falls\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Kauai Myanmar food & sushi\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Kapaa lookout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Safeway\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Explored the hotel\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Monday \u8226? 8-24-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up, ate leftover Babe\u8217?s chicken, relaxed in bed watching YouTube while playing games. When Val got home @12, we went to Val\u8217?s appointment @1, we then went home and cooked and ate lunch, then we took a nap. When Val got her eyebrows done I dropped off the cats @MD\u8217?s. Got home, went to the gym and hit legs together, then we went home, finished packing and had a late dinner. Excited for Hawaii :)\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Val\u8217?s doctor\u8217?s appointments\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dropped of Cats @MD\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Packed for Hawaii\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Sunday \u8226? 8-23-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up, made breakfast, watched YouTube while updating photos, then browed the internet relaxing in bed. We tried to go to Pho MC after Val got off from work but its closed on Sundays so we went to In n Out but decided to eat after working out. We ate dinner then went for a walk around the lake with Gabe, Marianne, and Mounika. Rescheduled a lunch with Kichang to another day next week.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Babe\u8217?s Chicken Dinner House\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Evening walk\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Saturday \u8226? 8-22-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up and ate oatmeal Val made for me. Then I left to Lowes to get the Lowes cup which was free, then headed over to vacuum my car @Quick Quack car wash. When I got home I spoke with the front office to find my Amazon package. They couldn\u8217?t find it in the mail room so I had to request a refund on Amazon. On the way to the front office I ran into Mounika and we spoke for a bit, went to her apartment to grab Steven\u8217?s towel and talked a bit about her new trip to New York and California. I then waited for Val to get home so I made lunch, fed the cats lunch, watched YouTube then headed out to get groceries @HEB. After we went home and headed to the gym. On the way into the apartment we saw Casey and decided to go to Schools with her. We walked around the store and stopped by Truckyard to get some food. We ended up not getting anything since Val wasn\u8217?t hungry so we went home and slept.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lowes\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Quick Quack Car Wash\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Spoke with Front office about Amazon package\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Socialized with Mounika\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   HEB\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Scheels\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Truckyard\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Friday \u8226? 8-21-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up, ate breakfast, unpacked the cooler, cleaned dishes, journaled, made a San Antonio vacation notion page, watched YouTube, calculated how much the New York and San Antonio trip costed, sorted photos, called Frontier for an update on the refund, napped, made lunch, hit the gym, showered, ate leftovers for dinner, and fed the cats. I\u8217?m getting more into history and understanding the history of the US. Learned more about the Mexican American war and the historic value of the Alamo. I\u8217?m going to attempt to get the free cup from Lowe\u8217?s tomorrow.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Called Frontier for refund\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Thursday \u8226? 8-20-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 3 in San Antonio. Woke up, ate free hotel breakfast then headed out for the day. Went to the San Antonio Botanical garden walking around and exploring the garden. It was nice but nothing breathtaking. While on our walk David Yang ft me and Matthew saying Haroon wanted to kill him self, he changed religion, and had sex with prostitutes. Lots of trauma dumping and I hope he is doing well. We then went to the World\u8217?s largest cowboy boots and went inside of the mall. We had a snack @Chick Fli La and then did some shopping for Val. It was a nice mall that I would actually go to but the layout was unique. We then left to go to a museum but we ended up paying for it since it was free from 4pm - 9pm. We then went to another museum for free that also had an outside park. We ate tacos @Birria Barrio, and I personally believe it was one of the best tacos I have ever had. We drove back to the hotel and took a nap. After we woke up, we packed everything we had and headed back to Dallas. Great trip to San Antonio, however I don\u8217?t think I\u8217?ll go back voluntarily. 14.4k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   San Antonio Botanical Garden\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Worlds Largest Cowboy Boots\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   North Star mall\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   McNay Art Museum\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Ruby City\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Birria Barrio\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Drove to Dallas\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Wednesday \u8226? 8-19-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 2 in San Antonio. Woke up and ate free hotel breakfast. Applied for unemployment and then went to go explore San Antonio by going to the San Fernando Cathedral. We walked over to the Historic Market Square. It was colorful and peaceful with many shops. There wasn\u8217?t too many people there since it was the middle of the week with not a lot of tourists. We then visited an art gallery on the way back to the car. Got to the car then went to HEB to grab some $7 sushi. We then went to the Mexican Cultural Institute, however they were closed till 1pm. We walked around for 15 mins and ran into these people asking for donations. I spoke with a guy who was from Atlanta who studied CS but I ended up not giving him donations since $30 was the minimum. We tried to go to the Mexican Cultural Institute @1:05pm and we see a sign that says closed till 2pm. We just left to go to another museum. We go to the museum and it was our first time seeing a black light exhibit. We then left to go look for food @Peral however we didn\u8217?t see anything we liked so we left to get some food @Gus\u8217?s World Famous Fried Chicken. After eating some fried chicken we went home and showered. Started watching National Geographic about octopus and bees. 10.8k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Applied for unemployment\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   San Fernando Cathedral\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Historic Market Square\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Centro de Artes Gallery\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   HEB\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Mexican Cultural Institute\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Contemporary at Blue Star\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pearl\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Gus\u8217?s World Famous Fried Chicken\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Tuesday \u8226? 8-18-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 1 in San Antonio. We woke up and ate free hotel breakfast. We then watched some National Geographic about beavers before leaving to explore San Antonio. We explored the Alamo and learned some history about the Alamo. We then explored some monuments in the area and bought some souvenirs. We then walked around the River Walk and the area is so nice to walk around. We then got some lunch at Cafe Ole which was a Mexican restaurant and they didn\u8217?t serve the complimentary chips and salsa. The waiter took too long so I left a small tip. We then walked along the River Walk to explore the Shops at Rivercenter mall and it was nice but I\u8217?ve seen more extreme malls. We then headed over to the Japanese Tea Garden and took a 40 min nap in the parking lot. The views at the Japanese Tea Garden were incredible and the best Japanese garden in Texas. We made our way to Witte Museum and explored the museum. After going to the Met in New York, every museum is now subpar. We got some burgers @Burger Boy and headed home to eat. The burger reminded me of Whataburger, it was a good burger but not the best I\u8217?ve had. We spent the rest of the day bed rotting on our phones and watching Family Guy. I also bought a neck fan for whenever I travel. I miss cable TV where you change channels searching for a good show to watch.  13.2k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   The Alamo\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Alamo Cenotaph Monument\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Gift shop\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   La Antorcha de la Amistad (Spanish for "The Torch of Friendship")\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   River walk\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Cafe Ole\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   River Walk\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Shops at Rivercenter\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Japanese Tea Garden\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Witte Museum\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Burger Boy\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Monday \u8226? 8-17-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up and ate leftover pizza. I like journaling in the Notes app instead of Apple\u8217?s journal app. I like how it has locations for every entry, however the Notes seems to be easier to access on Windows PCs and updates faster. Did some research on how to visit Vietnam, and took some notes on the topics I need to study for job hunting. I took a nap then got blood work done. It took an hour waiting just to get to my blood work which only took two minutes. Got home and Val suggested we go to San Antonio since she doesn\u8217?t work till Friday. We made lunch, packed, ate, watched Suits then headed out to San Antonio. 5 hr drive. We got to the hotel and had to pay an extra $80 for the pet fee.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Quest Diagnostics appointment\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Packed for San Antonio\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Drove to San Antonio\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Sunday \u8226? 8-16-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up, went to Manish\u8217?s place to pick up a suit, then went home and got a coffee from Pax & Beneficia Coffee. Got dressed then went to Adil\u8217?s wedding, got home then worked out with Val. We played basketball for the first time and she cooked my ass. We are finishing season 5 of Suits and it is getting good.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Picked up suit from Manish\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pax & Beneficia Coffee\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Adil\u8217?s wedding\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Saturday \u8226? 8-15-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Played Wizard 101 then went to HEB to get some supplies for the pool party, took a nap, then ate some chicken before the party started. Steven came early and I didn\u8217?t see my phone so he waited outside for 30 mins waiting for me to respond. We walked to 2 different convenient stores looking for ice, but we ended up having to go to 7-11 to grab some ice. We then went to the pool to start the party and it was a great time. We hung out, watched the fight, and ate pizza.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   HEB\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   7-11\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pool party\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Friday \u8226? 8-14-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up, made breakfast, made a sandwich and cut apples for Val to go to work, then played more Wizard 101 while watching Harry Mack videos. Then I went to the gym, came back, ate a late lunch, showered, played more Wizard 101, then went to sleep.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Thursday \u8226? 8-13-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up, made breakfast, played Wizard 101, then called and made an appointment for Kind Clinic, took a nap, got home, made dinner, cleaned dishes, watched Suits, played more Wizard 101, then went to sleep.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Scheduled Kind Clinic appointment\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Wednesday \u8226? 8-12-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Bean woke me up @5am and I couldn\u8217?t fall back asleep so I played Wizard 101 till 6am then woke up @9:30am. Didn\u8217?t go to the movies today so we stayed inside and chilled. We went to HEB to get new cutting boards since my old board was growing mold on them. We ate BBQ for lunch then went home and played more Wizard 101.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   HEB\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @True Texas BBQ\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Kind Clinic video appointment\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Tuesday \u8226? 8-11-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up and planned to go to Gen KBBQ but Val didn\u8217?t want to go anymore so we went to Costco to get eggs and got some extra groceries. I ate a turkey sandwich then we went to HEB to get a pregnancy test. Val isn\u8217?t pregnant. I then went to workout and went straight to Val\u8217?s house to wash our cars. We went home, showered, and went to sleep\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Costco\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   HEB\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Washed mine and Val\u8217?s car\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Monday \u8226? 8-10-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up and did some research in buying a portable charger then bought one for travel. Made breakfast then played Wizard 101. Went to workout and played basketball. Noticed that my blood pressure is going down and is at a healthy reading from my home blood pressure reader. I\u8217?ll have to check @ one in HEB. Did some research on traveling and where I want to go, then sorted the New York pictures on Notion. Then I went to Walmart to get MD a tumbler and some Dr Pepper. It was nice seeing everyone playing FIFA and we just chilled and talked all night. I dropped Hatem off at his apartment then I went home.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Walmart\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   MD birthday party\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Sunday \u8226? 8-9-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Relaxing day. Woke up and played Wizard 101. Val felt sick this morning so she went home early. I ate breakfast, then we took a nap and I played more Wizard 101. Made a late lunch and watched Suits. Got the munchies so I got Port of Peri Peri for dinner. Relaxing day playing games and getting further in Wizard 101. I am finally in Mirage as a level 118 death wizard.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Port of Peri Peri\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Saturday \u8226? 8-8-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up, made breakfast, then played Wizard 101 till Val got home @2pm. She got home, I took a nap, then we went to go workout. After getting home she watched her show and I played Wizard 101, ate leftovers and went to sleep.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Friday \u8226? 8-7-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up and played Wizard 101 while I watched the news. I did this until Val got home from work @11am. I went to HEB @11am to get some groceries, then went home and made lunch. We then took a nap on the futon and started prepping the food we were going to bring at the potluck dinner. We came @7:20pm and ate food and played Code Names. It was a fun night. We lost to the girls 2-1 bc Gabe made a silly mistake thinking one of the cards was ours but it was theirs.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   HEB\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Potluck dinner @Gabe & Marianne\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Thursday \u8226? 8-6-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up and I finally made it to Polaris. I played Wizard 101 and watched the news in the background. Living the unemployed life. Budgeted for this month and it is safe to say that I am slowly being wanting to work to make some money, but after my two trips to Hawaii and Vietnam. I made breakfast then kept playing my game. Whenever Val got home I took a mini 20 min nap then went to go pick up her Avita medicine and go workout. After working out we went home and went on a walk around Lake Carolyn with Val & Mounika. It was nice socializing for a bit, but it was quite hot, even in the shade. We sat on a bench and talked for ~30 mins. We then went home, got a hair trim, showered, then made dinner\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Budget\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Picked up Val's medicine\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Evening walk ft. Mounika\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Wednesday \u8226? 8-5-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up and played Wizard 101. Applied for unemployment and then went to HEB for groceries for the week. Cleaned around the house doing dishes, putting up groceries, doing litter, making lunch and eating lunch while watching Black Mirror. Then bought some items from Amazon, called Frontier for a refund and they said it will take up to 7 business days for an email with an amount refunded to show up. Went to go workout, dropped Val off to her house to pick up her car, then we made dinner and watched Black Mirror while I played Wizard 101.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Applied for unemployment\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   HEB\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Chores\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Called Frontier for refund\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dropped Val off @ her house\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Tuesday \u8226? 8-4-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Last day in New York. We didn\u8217?t do anything in New York since we had to be at the airport at a reasonable time. We took the subway to the airport, then hopped on our flight. It only had a 30 min delay which wasn\u8217?t bad but we ended up getting to Dallas safe and sound. Gabe picked us up from the airport, we got home, ate some small snacks then went to go pick up Obama & Bean. We were so excited to see them and we talked to MD about his experience. It seemed like he enjoyed having them a lot and would want to have them back again. We then spent the rest of our day unpacking, washing clothes, folding clothes, eating pizza, then watching Black Mirror to end the night.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Flight to Dallas\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Picked up Obama & Bean\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Chores\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Watched Black Mirror\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Dominos\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Monday \u8226? 8-3-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 6 in New York. Woke up and ate breakfast Connor made for us. Then we went to the Met. It was wet and slightly raining outside so we brought two umbrellas. We spent ~3.5 hours in the museum taking pictures and walking around, we couldn\u8217?t go to the Moma Museum. We will just have to go next time. We ended up going to Saigon Shack and took Central Park on the way there. It was nice and scenic and we stopped by Belvedere Castle where I got a pin. We made it to Saigon Shack and got pho bo. It was mid and expensive. Also got a Thai tea which was also mid, but refreshing. We then walked around Soho for Val so that she could go shopping and I supported her like a great boyfriend. We then went to Canal street and I was looking for some rings. When we got there, there was someone who was trying to steal a ring from a seller and their other friends helped him out. We walked around and did some sightseeing, then went to the Jenga Tower to take some pics and sit down. We then watched the sunset @Rockefeller Park and sat on a bench where Val got scared of a rat and screamed, making me jump out of my seat. We then met up with Connor & Michelle and walked around the city then went home to rest after. 24.3k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   The Metropolitan Museum of Art\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Belvedere Castle\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Saigon Shack\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Soho\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Canal street\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Jenga Tower\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Rockefeller Park\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Sunday \u8226? 8-2-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 5 in New York. Ate eggs, avocado and sweet tomatoes with a coffee. Shoutout to Connor & Michelle. We left to Coney Island to ride the rides, view and beach and walk the pier. Spent $180 for all day passes and used up 250 credits, meaning we made our money\u8217?s worth. We got some chicken tenders @Nathan\u8217?s and it\u8217?s been open for 100+ years. My favorite ride was the Colossal and we rode it 3 times in a row. There was a person selling pics with a Kinkajou and me and Val got our money\u8217?s worth. After Coney Island, we went to Canal street and got a bag for Val, a card holder, and belt for me. Long day at Coney Island, but at least we did it and crossed it off of our list. 17k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Paid rent\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Coney Island\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Nathan\u8217?s\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pics w Kinkajou\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Canal street\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Saturday \u8226? 8-1-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 4 in New York. Woke up in the middle of the night from Justin\u8217?s friends coming over @2am. Went to sleep after and woke up and left to go to Connor\u8217?s place. We talked and caught up for a bit then headed to brunch @Westville Dumbo. Brunch was good, conversation was rolling then we headed to Dumbo to take some pictures and a get an old newspaper souvenir. We then walked to a Jane\u8217?s Carousel. Took pictures in the area but then Michelle had to leave to go meet up with her patient. We then walked and talked around the park and ended up heading to the Statue of Liberty. We took a subway back to Manhattan but we stopped by the charging bull and took pics with a snake. Best pictures of the trip by far and worth the money. We then got tickets to Statue of Liberty and got into line. The wait took a bit of time but we were able to get on the island and go to the Statue of Liberty Museum. It was cool to view but nothing worth spending money on. It was free so that was a plus. We headed back which surprisingly didn\u8217?t take as long as I anticipated. We got back into Manhattan and walked around the Battery and saw the Sea Glass Carousel and Connor said it looks like shit lmaoooo. We took pictures of the statues in the area and Connor left us to go to a house warming party. Me and Val then headed to get a beer with Miguel, Gummy, and Sami @Jeremy\u8217?s Ale House. It was cool talking and catching up with them. They went to go get pasta and me and Val went to go walk the Brooklyn Bridge. It was nice to view the bridge at night and a good choice to walk it at night. It was still busier than I expected @10:30pm. We then went to Canal street to watch some police raids however the sellers weren\u8217?t out today. So we headed to Times Square. We got lost on the way to Times Square since there was a delay on one of the subways so we did some circling around but eventually made it to Times Square ~11:50pm. We watched the show, which was mid, then head home back to Connor\u8217?s place. On the way back we went to a deli and got some chips to snack on. Showered and went to sleep to get ready for the next day. 23.7k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Go to Connor\u8217?s place\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Brunch @Westville Dumbo\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dumbo\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Charging Bull\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pics w snake\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Statue of Liberty\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Statue of Liberty Museum\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Sea Glass Carousel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   East Coast Memorial\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Titanic Memorial Park\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Beer @Jeremy\u8217?s Ale House\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Brooklyn Bridge\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Canal street\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Times Square\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Friday \u8226? 7-31-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 3 in New York. Ate leftovers for breakfast, washed dishes, then left the apartment by 11am. Getting better at finding directions for the subway but still not perfect. Arrived at the Oculus World Trade Center mall and there were food vendors outside selling food. All different types of food but prices were quite expensive. We then saw both of the 9/11 water memorials. We took pictures of the sculptures outside then went to the Mercer Labs. We spent ~$100 @Mercer Labs, it was a cool experience but personally I do not think it was worth +$100. We got a snack from a Filipino BBQ vendor where we got a chicken BBQ, pork belly BBQ, and beef BBQ skewer. Pork belly was me and Val\u8217?s personal favorite. After eating our snack we went to the 9/11 museum and spent 3.5 hours there. We came in @2:30pm and left @6pm. We felt hungry so we went to get pizza at a random pizza spot called Stage Door Pizza. Each slice was $5.50 which isn\u8217?t bad, but I believe there is cheaper prices in the area. Val really wanted to go to Canal street and see some fake designer bags. So we headed straight to Canal street. On the way we saw a bit of China town, saw $1.50 pizza, and felt the quality of the city go down. Trash around the area, the Africans selling on the corners and cops patrolling the area. I bought a LV wallet and tried to get some rings but as I was trying on some rings, the cops ran up on us and arrested someone. It was crazy and chaotic. We walked around the block another time and walked into another gift shop to get some souvenirs. Definitely need to come back again to get a ring. We headed home and got some chips and tea at a local deli. Showered and talked to Justin for a bit before relaxing in bed for the rest of the night. 14.8k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Food market outside Oculus World Trade Center\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   9/11 Memorial\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Oculus World Trade Center\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Mercer Labs\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Snack @Food market outside Oculus World Trade Center\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   9/11 Museum\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Stage Door Pizza\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Canal Street\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   New York gift shop\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Snack & drinks @Deli\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Thursday \u8226? 7-30-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 2 in New York. Woke up earlier then went to a deli with Miguel and got a bacon, egg, hash brown, and cheese with mayo and ketchup. It rained on us so we ran back home. We left the apartment and when to the public library. After touring the whole library we went to the gift shop/cafe in the library. I had an interaction with this older guy who didn\u8217?t seem to speak English. I saw a self balancing bird and I picked it up from the balancing stand. He looked at me and gave me a nod of approval, then I put it back. I then pick up the box and point at the price tag and shook my head with disapproval. He gave me a slight chuckle and we both when our separate paths. We then walked to the Grand Central Terminal. We took pics then left. As we were leaving we found a New York Transit Museum. This was small but had a couple of unique artwork inside. There was a street performer there as well playing the guitar. We headed over to the St. Patrick\u8217?s Cathedral which also had insane architecture. Lots of religious artwork and beautiful glass panels, but a great place to visit. We lit a candle and used this time to rest for a bit in AC. By this time it started sprinkling and we quickly rushed to Rockefeller Center. Wasn\u8217?t much to it, just an outdoor plaza with tables and a cafe. We took shelter in a New York gift shop. Bought a magnet and avoided the rain for a bit. We then wanted to visit the Museum of Modern Art, however there was a line outside, even in the rain, so I just bought a hot dog and ate it on the ground next to the Museum of Modern Art Design store. This was my first time having sauerkraut and I thought it was alright. We visited the Modern Art Design store and I liked the umbrella dryer they had there. We then visited the Louis Vuitton 200 Trucks Exhibition and it was pretty cool seeing art like this. However it was rusting a bit and it was cloudy so it wasn\u8217?t a 10/10 picture I took. We left to the Museum of Arts & Design and it had some cool exhibits. Val tried to put the umbrella into an umbrella protector that didn\u8217?t have any plastic and it made the security guard laugh. The museum was having an event showing off the new movie The Devil Wears Prada 2. They had to office on the 6th floor and clothes and a walk way on the 7th floor. We left and were planning on going to Central Park but I got a hot dog first. After eating two hot dogs from stands, I do not want to eat another hot dog. Each were $5 and they were both mid. Next time I need to try a pizza. We stopped by Popeyes to get Val some wings and me a chicken wrap. While we were eating two black kids were trolling a grown middle eastern man. The kids asked the guy if they could have a $20 but the guy said to call him daddy. I asked the guy what happened and the guy said the kids were in the way and said \u8220?move out the way daddy\u8221?. I think his response was kind weird but that probably started a whole interaction. We spent the rest of the daylight we had in Central park, roaming around the park, rocks, and enjoying the greenery. We ended up heading home around 8:30pm and I took the wrong subway to get home. First mistake on using the subway. Lesson learned. The corner entrances matter. As we arrived to the subway station, Val noticed a man with a fake dog. This was a content creator named J-Massiah and I asked him if he was the content creator with the fake dog scaring people. He said he was just holding it for someone. I left and looked him up and Val confirmed it was him. I then came back and asked for a picture. After getting a picture we finally got on a subway. There were delays in the subway which caused long lines in the subway stations and long waits in the subways before they could take off. This is my first bad experience in public transportation here in NY. Val saw Miguel in the corner of the same subway we got on which the odds of that happening is insane. We walked home together and stoped by a Chinese restaurant for Miguel. I got a wonton soup to help chow down my leftovers from this morning. Showered and ended the night chilling in bed and reflecting on the day. 27k steps.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Breakfast @Deli\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   New York Public Library\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Grand Central Terminal\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   New York Transit Museum\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   St. Patrick\u8217?s Cathedral\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Rockefeller Center\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nintendo New York\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   New York Gifts\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hot dog @Hot dog stand\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Museum of Modern Art Design Store\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Louis Vuitton 200 Trunks Exhibition\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Museum of Arts & Design\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Hot dog @Hot dog stand\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch for Val @Popeyes\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Central Park\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wonton soup @Ten Full\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Wednesday \u8226? 7-29-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 1 in New York. Late morning due to catching up on sleep the night before. Left the place around 11am and went to get lunch and Thai tea @Thai Tree NYC. We then took the subway to Vessel. The scenery is amazing in this area. It\u8217?s nice and there is a lot of greenery in the area. Went to The Shops after visiting the Vessel. The shops are 5 stories high with great stores. I could imagine myself going to this mall just to walk around. I bought a Uniqlo cap and then made our way to the Edge NYC on the fourth floor to get a view of the whole city. The view is insane coming from a Houston/Dallas city. Went to the Shed and it was free but boring. They had a movie playing and I thought there would be an exhibit like a museum. We walked the High Line which is an abandoned railroad that turned into a park. Lots of greenery in New York which is a huge plus. On the way we saw a huge man-made island which caught our attention. There was a piano out in public and kids were playing on it and a rehearsal going on at a pavilion. We sat and watched the show for a bit then checked out Pier 57. It was a nice indoor area and there were a lot of people running in the area. We went to go meet up with Miguel @Chelsea Market and got some food @Very Fresh Noodles then walked to Little Island to eat. After we ate, we went back to the Chelsea Market to get some mango sticky rice. It was sweet and the first time I\u8217?ve tried mango sticky rice. Would definitely get it again. We talked and walked home and on the way home we got a glimpse of Times Square which had a bunch of shops on lights that lit up the night. Stopped by Target to buy a towel. The city never sleeps. 23k steps today.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Thai Tree NYC\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Vessel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   The Shops\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Edge NYC\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   The Shed\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   The High Line\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Little Island\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pier 57\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Chelsea Market\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Very Fresh Noodles\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Little Island\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Target\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Tuesday \u8226? 7-28-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up @5am to catch our flight @7:50am, just to have it delayed to 10:28am. Ended up circling above the airport for an hour with 10 planes above us so we stopped @Philadelphia. Got there around 4pm and stayed till 9:30pm. We ended up going on public transportation and went on an adventure just to get to Miguel\u8217?s apartment. Interacted with an asian in a suit and boots who asked for a pen to journal. After going on 4+ subways and a 0.5 mile walk, we made it to Miguel\u8217?s apartment @1am.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Flight to Philadelphia\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Burger King\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Train to 30th Street Station\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Train to New York Moynihan Train Hall @Penn Station\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Monday \u8226? 7-27-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Grind Wizard 101 while Val went to work. Packed for NY. Then went to help Mounika visit her apartment and gave her my cart to help her move. We then left to drop off Bean & Obama to MD. Went to HEB to get some last minute travel supplies and coffee. Then went to Mounika\u8217?s old apartment to help her move. We finished the night @Gabe & Marianne\u8217?s apartment eating Popeye chicken wings and pizza. Went home and made sure everything was packed for our early flight tomorrow.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Packing for NY\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Gave Mounika cart\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dropped off cats @MD\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   HEB\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Helped Mounika move\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Sunday \u8226? 7-26-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up @6 from Bean rubbing his head on me, then went back to sleep to wake up @10am. Played Wizard 101 until Val got home. She took a nap while I played Wizard 101. Currently farming the Darkmoor dungeon for gear. I made food, did chores, and spent the day recovering from drinking the night before.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Saturday \u8226? 7-25-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Played Wizard 101 all day. When Val got home we took a nap then worked out. Workout was cut short since we had to get dinner w Val's friends but I was able to do my entire workout in a short time. Me and Val got there early so we enjoyed the weather and some live music. We pregamed in Cynthia's car with cutwater then went to get some food @Yard House. Went home, showered, then fell asleep.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Yard House\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Friday \u8226? 7-24-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Lots of Wizard 101 today. A great morning playing Wizard 101 while watching YouTube. Val had brunch with her sisters so I had more time to myself playing Wizard 101. We went to your Mounika\u8217?s new apartment at our apartment complex. It was nice and we talked for a bit but I forgot to get Mounika our cart. When Val got home I had a late workout sesh which was a good way to stay productive.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Mounika's apartment tour\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Thursday \u8226? 7-23-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up and played Wizard 101 in the morning. Made breakfast then went to get groceries @HEB. Went home and did a deep cleaning of the apartment. Dishes, wiped counters, vacummed, mopped, cleaned toilet, cleaned bathroom sink, cleaned shower, laundry, and cat litter. Napped then went to the Shordie Shordie concert. Drank a beer which was a bad idea and made me need to pee which left me unconfortable during the performance.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   HEB\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Clean\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Shordie Shordie concert\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Wednesday \u8226? 7-22-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up and made progress in Wizard 101 and Clash of Clans. Finished upgrading all of my walls in Wizard 101. Then we went to Winspear Opera House to get some box office tickets. Waited for ~3 hours in the heat with slight AC. I saw some sculptures so I took pics. After getting the tickets we went to the mall to get a top for Val. Went home and took a nap while Val got ready. We went to the concert then after we got tacos @Salsa Verde. Very eventful day doing unemployed activities.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Applied for unemployment\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Clash of Clans grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Waited for Not for Radio tickets @Winspear Opera House\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Galleria\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Smoothie @Thirsty\u8217?s\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Not for Radio concert\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Salsa Verde\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Tuesday \u8226? 7-21-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Slow morning w Val. Made breakfast, did chores, watched Suits for a bit then took a nap. Studied Vietnamese then played more wizard 101.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Studied Vietnamese\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Monday \u8226? 7-20-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up and played Wizard 101. Made and went to a vet appointment. They were filled so I went to a different vet. Everyone loved Obama\u8217?s name. Did the litter, eye drops for Obama, called to ship the medication and played Wizard 101 while I watched YouTube until Val got home from work. Took a nap then woke up and played Wizard 101 again. Great relaxing day inside.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Vet appointment for Obama\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Chores\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Sunday \u8226? 7-19-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up @5:30am to catch my 6:45am bus to Dallas. It wasn\u8217?t bad but I was starting to get a headache. I got an Uber to HEB and spoke with a guy who recently got a gig selling software sales. Tipped well and met up w Val @HEB to do some grocery shopping for the week. Got home and checked out my new Oakley sunglasses, put up the groceries, and unpacked a bit. We met up with Steven, Hatem, MD, UD, and MD\u8217?s siblings to watch the World Cup game @Texas Live. Spain beat Argentina. We were so tired so we left around 5:30pm. We got home, showered and unpacked a bit more before taking a nap.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Bus ride to Dallas\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   HEB\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   World Cup Finals @Texas Live\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Unpacked\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Watched Kaleidoscope\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Saturday \u8226? 7-18-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Drove back from Florida. Fun trip. On the way back we stopped by Raising Canes for lunch. Didn\u8217?t do much today since I spent 8 hours on the road. When I got home dad bought a massage chair for $14 at an auction. Spent the rest of the day playing Wizard 101 and prepping for my trip back to Dallas.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Drove to Houston\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Raising Canes\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Friday \u8226? 7-17-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 5 in Florida. Woke up, had breakfast. Then we went to Pensacola Beach. This time we parked on the side of the road and walked about a mile to find a spot at the beach. We found a spot, watched the show and this intrigued my interest in air shows. We went to Andy D\u8217?s restaurant however there was a 30 min wait and it was already 5pm. Everyone was tired and hungry, even I felt fatigued from pushing & pulling the wagon. We went home and ate ramen & eggs, then showered and went to Navarre Beach to take pics. Cody drew a huge penis in the sand and then we went home. They bought snow crab and we had a second dinner and it was great. I packed for Houston then went to sleep. Long day at the beach.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pensacola Beach\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Blue Angels Air Show\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Navarre Beach pics\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Thursday \u8226? 7-16-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 4 in Florida. Woke up, had breakfast. Then we went to Pensacola Beach. However we had issues with parking costing around $50 and saw one with $100 due to the Blue Angels air show. We stopped by Alvin\u8217?s Island and I got a magnet and snow globe. We then drove back to Navarre Beach where I chilled in the shade all day since I was getting a bit burnt on my shoulders. I dug a hole and stretched while hanging out on my phone. I enjoyed the weather and laid in the sand while Cody and Cong went fishing on the pier. Drove home and ate dinner. I bed rotted the rest of the day.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pensacola Beach\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Alvin\u8217?s Island\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Walmart\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Navarre Beach\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Wednesday \u8226? 7-15-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 3 in Florida. Woke up around 7:30am and had breakfast. We left to Destin around 11am and it took about 55ish mins to get there. When we got there, finding parking was a hassle. However we got lucky and found a spot in public parking right when someone left their spot. We then walked to eat at Pompano Joe\u8217?s. I got a seafood combo which had fried oysters, fried fish, fried scallops, fried shrimp, hush puppies, crab cake, baked potato, and french fries. It was ~$45 but it was paid for. Muwahaha. After lunch, we hit the beach. We setup the canopy which was a first for me, then we boogie boarded and chilled under the canopy. We did this for about 5-6 hours then left. We stopped by Bass Pro Shop where me and Cody looked at fishing gear and guns. We also stopped at Whole Foods to get some groceries as well. It took about 1.5 hours to get back to the AirBnb. Once we got back, we showered, I ate my leftovers, texted Val, and chilled on the couch. Long day in Destin however it was great for my first time.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Destin Beach\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Bass Pro Shop\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Whole Foods\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Tuesday \u8226? 7-14-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 2 in Florida. Woke up, had breakfast, then went to the beach to fish and go to the beach. After 3 hours of fishing\u8230? I caught nothing lmaoo. So I went to the beach and boogie boarded for a while. It was nice to boogie board again because I haven\u8217?t done it in so long. We chilled in the shade playing in the sand and messing with the birds. There was a sea turtle hatching site nearby and we couldn\u8217?t enter the area since the sea turtle eggs were already laid. While we were chilling in the shade, there was a flying canopy flying towards us. Two of the legs broke off and I ran away but we stopped it with a bunch of randoms. We left around 2pm and got home and showered. I played Wizard 101 and watched Tik Toks & reels to past the time. After an eventful first half of the day, it was nice to relax for the evening. I have also come to realize that there is not much to do in Navarre/Destin. Once you spend a week here doing everything the city has to offer. There aren\u8217?t many great food spots besides American food.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Fishing @Navarre Beach Fishing Pier\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Navarre Beach\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Monday \u8226? 7-13-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 1 in Florida. Woke up @5am and left Houston @6am. We arrived in Navarre near Destin around 4:30pm. We chilled for a bit then went to Navarre Beach where they had a pier and beach. Caitlyn drew a penis and these random guys came up and laughed about it. We then walked the fishing pier and Cong saw an old fishing friend he saw last time he went fishing. Went home, showered and ate dinner. Quick grocery run to pick up essentials like ice cream, chopsticks and beer. Went home and played Wizard 101. Not much today since it was spent on the road but a solid first day.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Drove to Florida from Houston\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Florida Welcome Center\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Navarre Beach\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Groceries @Publix\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Sunday \u8226? 7-12-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 4 in Houston. After getting gas, Val and I changed our minds on the way to the Galleria and headed to Kemah Boardwalk instead. We walked around Kemah Boardwalk. We went to feed stingrays and viewed the mini aquarium they had. We got tickets to the Boardwalk Beast Speedboat. It was slightly raining so it was painful to open your eyes since the raindrops would sting your face. Looking to the side of the boat helped but not much. Next time, I\u8217?d go when it\u8217?s sunny or bring sunglasses when it\u8217?s raining. We went home, napped and watched Kaleidoscope. We binged it for a while until we had to pack all of our things for Florida. Great way to end our trip to Houston. Onto Florida!\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Kemah Boardwalk\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Watched Kaleidoscope\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Packed for Florida\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Saturday \u8226? 7-11-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 3 in Houston. A nice day in Houston. Ate breakfast then met up with Rajiv at the POST. Showed him around Herman Park where parking was terrible. After he left me and Val went to the Asia Society Texas Center for free. Went home and napped. We woke up and binged Kaleidoscope. Great show that you can apparently watch in any order.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   The POST\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Herman Park\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Asia Society Texas Center\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Watched Kaleidoscope\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Friday \u8226? 7-10-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 2 in Houston. Ate breakfast and spoke with my parents talking about communism, Vietnam and life. Went to Meow Wolf in Houston and took some pictures next to Meow Wolf. Got fries and a milkshake at Buttermilk Baby then drove home to nap and get ready for Kamel\u8217?s wedding.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Meow Wolf\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Photo Booth Museum\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Buttermilk Baby\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Kamel\u8217?s Wedding\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Thursday \u8226? 7-9-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 1 in Houston. Drove to Houston, got a car inspection, went to the wrong Annex, then got the inspection sticker, unpacked extra clothes, took a nap, spent time with family, got a haircut, threw out trash for Mom, got dry cat food, ate dinner with my parents, and ended the night watching Netflix. A great first day in Houston.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Drove to Houston\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Car inspection @Take 5\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Car inspection sticker @Galveston County Clerk Annex\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Haircut\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   HEB\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Wednesday \u8226? 7-8-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Applied for unemployment. Did research on which cat dry food to buy and what cabin sized suitcase to buy. Worked out and went to eat Popeyes for dinner. Made the last minute decision to leave in the morning instead of leaving at night.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Applied for unemployment\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Popeyes\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pack for Houston\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Tuesday \u8226? 7-7-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up productive and excited for our New York trip. Created my Austin trip page on Notion and grind Wizard 101 in the morning. Went to get food and coffee while Val studied and I played Wizard 101. Steven stopped by to pick up the cats and talked for a bit. It\u8217?s getting easier to talk to him. We had to go to Mounika\u8217?s to celebrate her getting a new job. It was nice to socialize with friends and eat free pizza and wings.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Added Austin trip to Notion\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @In-N-Out\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Coffee @Pax & Beneficia Coffee\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Steven picked up Kiki & Kumo\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Mounika\u8217?s\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Monday \u8226? 7-6-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 5 of having 4 cats. Each cat has their own personalities. Kumo is finally starting to become affectionate, Obama is getting distant, Bean plays with cats instead of humans, Kiki still hangs with humans. Kiki is probably the most affectionate, maybe because she is still a kitten.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Studied Vietnamese\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Watched Suits\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Sunday \u8226? 7-5-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 4 of having 4 cats. It\u8217?s becoming a new normal. It loud but hissing stopped, except when Bean & Kiki play with each other. Studied Vietnamese today and I have to keep the momentum going. Walked to Pax & Beneficia Coffee to get a Chai drink, then sat outside and watched security give someone a ticket/warning. Great Sunday spent.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Studied Vietnamese\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pax & Beneficia Coffee\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Watched Suits\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Saturday \u8226? 7-4-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 3 of having 4 cats. It just gets nosier. Bean and Kiki play with each other, Kiki hisses at Bean but it is decreasing as time goes on. Obama plays with Kumo occasionally. Kiki hisses less now and plays with Bean a lot. Grinding Wizard 101 and currently in Avalon. Tried a new dish at Abe Japanese restaurant however I didn\u8217?t like the noodles. At least I tried something new. Me and Val tried to see fireworks @Fair Park & Klyde Warren Park however they cancelled fireworks @Fair Park and there was too much traffic at Clyde Warren Park so we just went home and watched Suits.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dinner @Abe Japanese Restaurant\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Attempt to see fireworks @Fair Park & Klyde Warren Park\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Watched Suits\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Friday \u8226? 7-3-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Day 2 of having 4 cats and it\u8217?s chaotic. Bean and Kiki were cuddling for a bit during the night. Obama is curious about Kiki. Kumo is a bit more skittish now. Kiki likes to hang with humans. Bean focuses his attention playing with Kiki while Kiki doesn\u8217?t really like it. Kiki is a little spicy but with time I think she will get used to the other cats.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Budget\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Coffee w Junho @Pax & Beneficia Coffee\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Ft w Miguel\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   HEB\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Sparks & Stripes Fireworks w Gabe & Marianne\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Thursday \u8226? 7-2-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Went to the mall and bought Oakley sunglasses and Puma shoes for Val. Walked around and went to a park with Teddy Bears in Dallas. We then picked up Kumo and met Steven\u8217?s new cat Kiki and brought them home. Day 1 of taking care of 4 cats. Dined in at Babes for the first time and it was amazing.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   North Park mall\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lakeside Park\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pickup Kumo & Kiki from Steven\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Babe\u8217?s\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Wednesday \u8226? 7-1-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Productive day grinding Wizard 101. Worked out, ran errands and enjoyed the day.  Played Wizard 101 while Val was studying for her exam at Starbucks. Lots of progress in Wizard 101, almost done with Zafaria.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Amazon pickup @Whole Foods\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Pay rent\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Starbucks\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Tuesday \u8226? 6-30-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Another great stress-free day. I have thoughts of prepping to get a job however I am locked in at being unlocked.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dropped of Val @HEB\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Green tea @Starbucks\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Picked up Val @HEB\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Watched Suits\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Monday \u8226? 6-29-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Picked up medicine for Val and went to the House of Flavor in Dallas. It was nice to get free wings and fries. Took pictures and went to Cafe Olivia to do some work, drink coffee and use free Wifi. We then window shopped at North Park. Now I am into Oakley's sunglasses.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Picked up medicine for Val\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   House of Flavor by Wingstop\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Caf\u233? Olivia\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   North Park Mall\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Sunday \u8226? 6-28-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Finished Celestia, on Azteca in Wizard 101. Mom called and spoke to me in Vietnamese while I tried to speak in Vietnamese. Went to the Galleria Mall and walked around with Val after we had lunch. Then went to a basketball meetup with DFriga and Coach Gremlin. Friga didn't play but I got pictures with the hoopers.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Wizard 101 grind\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   1 hour phone call with Mom\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Galleria Mall\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @5 Guys\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Smoothie @Thirsty's\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Basketball meetup\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Saturday \u8226? 6-27-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Heavy Wizard 101 grind. Val worked from 6am - 4:30pm so she had a long day. Whenever she got home