e running errands and going to museums by myself. The Arlington Museum of Art was mid and I wouldn\u8217?t come here again, probably because they had mid exhibitions during this time. However as I was walking out, I saw the National Metal of Honor museum which was by far one of the best museums I have ever been to. The architecture was incredible and I spent more time than I thought I would here. They had this room where they have pre-recorded questions and answers from these metal of honor recipients which was by far the coolest feature of the museum. After Val got home from work, it was a chill day. I need to find more productive activities to do at home.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Morning run\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Return Amazon packages\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Arlington Museum of Art\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   National Metal of Honor museum\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Replace gate key\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Studied chess\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Wednesday \u8226? 5-13-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 A day well spent doing the things I enjoyed. Me and Val went to the Dallas World aquarium which was larger than I thought. We walked to El Fenix and it was my first time eating at this restaurant. It was for a great price for the amount of food we received. I would definitely come here again. We both crashed on the couch. Nap was a bit long however I do what I want now lol.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Morning walk\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dallas World Aquarium\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @El Fenix\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Kind clinic appointment\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Studied chess\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Tuesday \u8226? 5-12-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 First day where I felt like I needed to do more. Yes I was productive working out, going on walks around the lake. However, I need to fill in the empty space with hobbies/activities to keep me busy.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Morning walk\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Applied for unemployment\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Workout\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Evening walk\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Monday \u8226? 5-11-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Great way to start the first day of unemployment by doing the things I enjoy.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Walk\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Sort wedding photos\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Dallas Holocaust and Human Rights Museum\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Steve picked up Kumo\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Sunday \u8226? 5-10-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Rajiv\u8217?s & Sarika\u8217?s Wedding had us busy all day.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Rajiv\u8217?s wedding\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch @Mi Cocina\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Rajiv\u8217?s reception\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Saturday \u8226? 5-9-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Parents visit so most of my attention was on them. Couldn\u8217?t do much.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Parents visit\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch w parents @Cheddars\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Nap\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Parents leave\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Evening walk\par \li0\fi0 \par \b Friday \u8226? 5-8-2026\b0\par \li0\fi0 Woke up to a nice surprise. Spent all day socializing with coworkers by going to lunch with all of the ex-Paycom employees. Then met up with Rise @4 for a beer. After Mengrui left me, Gabe, and Manish walked around Cypress waters where we talked about each other and our time at Paycom.\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Laid off\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Lunch w Ex-Paycom coworkers @Flying Saucer\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Beers w Rise @Flying Saucer\par \li0\fi0 \u8211?   Afternoon walk with Gabe + Manish\par \li0\fi0 \par }